E["npc:darion-mograine"] = {t="npc",n="Darion Mograine",z="easternplaguelands",s="Darion Mograine is the younger son of the fallen Highlord Alexandros Mograine, the legendary Ashbringer. A former paladin who joined the Argent Dawn following his father's mysterious downfall, Darion's desperate quest to uncover his family's fate placed him at the center of the conflict consuming the Plaguelands.",h="Darion Mograine is the younger son of the fallen Highlord Alexandros Mograine, the legendary Ashbringer.",sec={{t="A Son of the Silver Hand",b="Darion grew up in the shadow of his father's towering legacy. Raised near Brill in the kingdom of Lordaeron, he witnessed the onset of the plague of undeath and eventually took up arms as a recruit in the Knights of the Silver Hand during the Third War. After falling in battle at Stratholme and narrowly surviving, Darion's world unraveled when his father perished under suspicious circumstances. Struggling with grief and questioning his faith in the Holy Light, Darion chose a different road than the zealous Scarlet Crusade, ultimately throwing his lot in with the newly formed Argent Dawn.",sp=0},{t="The Quest for the Ashbringer",b="Spurred on by cryptic omens, Darion led a desperate expedition into the dread necropolis Naxxramas to find the truth behind his father's fate. He discovered Alexandros raised as a death knight in service to the Scourge. Though he reclaimed his father's corrupted blade, the blade's restless whispers revealed his brother Renault's bitter betrayal. Darion sought the counsel of the exiled paladin Tirion Fordring, who warned him that only an act of profound love could redeem his father's tormented soul.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Darion Mograine?",a="Darion is a human warrior and paladin of the Argent Dawn, and the younger son of Highlord Alexandros Mograine, the original wielder of the legendary Ashbringer blade.",al={"darion mograine lore","who is darion","mograine son"}},{q="Why didn't Darion join the Scarlet Crusade like his brother?",a="While his elder brother Renault climbed the ranks of the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, Darion grew disillusioned with zealotry after their father's death. Guided by outside counsel and seeking genuine redemption rather than blind fury, Darion pledged his sword to the more inclusive Argent Dawn instead.",al={"darion scarlet crusade","why argent dawn darion"}},{q="What is Darion's connection to the Ashbringer?",a="Darion witnessed the creation of the blade as a youth in Southshore. After his father's death, Darion infiltrated Naxxramas and recovered the tainted greatsword in hopes of freeing Alexandros's bound spirit.",al={"darion and the ashbringer","did darion get the sword"},sp=1},{q="What advice did Tirion Fordring give him?",a="When Darion sought out the exiled Tirion Fordring for help cleansing the corrupted blade, Tirion told him that nothing ordinary could save Alexandros, and that only an act of love greater than the evil done to him could ever redeem his soul.",al={"tirion and darion","fordring advice darion"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Darion represents the deep crisis of faith paladins faced following the fall of Lordaeron, struggling to balance duty to the Light with the grim realities of the Plaguelands.",["race:Human"]="The tragic splintering of the Mograine household mirrors the ruin of Lordaeron itself, dividing brothers into rival orders amid the kingdom's ashes."},kw={"alexandros","argent dawn","ashbringer","darion mograine","naxxramas","renault","silver hand"},rel={"topic:argent-dawn","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","npc:tirion-fordring","npc:lord-maxwell-tyrosus","subzone:stratholme","topic:scourge","zone:easternplaguelands"},src={"Darion Mograine"}}
E["npc:lord-maxwell-tyrosus"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Maxwell Tyrosus",z="easternplaguelands",s="Lord Maxwell Tyrosus is the supreme commander of the Argent Dawn, stationed at their forward redoubt of Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands. A veteran paladin of the Silver Hand from the Third War, he guides the coalition's crusade against the Scourge and orchestrates strikes into blighted strongholds like Stratholme.",h="Lord Maxwell Tyrosus is the supreme commander of the Argent Dawn, stationed at their forward redoubt of...",sec={{t="A Veteran of Lordaeron",b="Maxwell Tyrosus rode alongside Uther the Lightbringer during the catastrophic Third War, guarding the exits of Andorhal when the Scourge tore through the kingdom. Following the fall of Lordaeron, he joined Highlord Alexandros Mograine in Hearthglen to sustain the resistance against the undead. Even then, Tyrosus advocated for unity across all races, intervening when zealous comrades like Brigitte Abbendis attempted to execute outsiders such as the troll priest Zabra Hexx. When Alexandros was betrayed and the remnants of the Silver Hand degenerated into the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, Tyrosus refused to follow their descent into xenophobia and broke away to help establish the Argent Dawn.",sp=0},{t="Commander of the Dawn",b="Following the death of Lord Raymond George, Tyrosus assumed leadership of the Argent Dawn. He welcomed Darion Mograine into the fold at Chillwind Point and later oversaw the defensive fortifications of Light's Hope Chapel. During the brutal Siege of the Sanguine, Tyrosus dealt a devastating blow to Kirkessen the Zealous, permanently shattering the lich's corporeal shell. From his command post within the chapel, he oversees broad military operations across the Plaguelands, including tactical assaults led by Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff against Baron Rivendare inside the ruins of Stratholme.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Maxwell Tyrosus?",a="Lord Maxwell Tyrosus is a veteran human paladin and the supreme leader of the Argent Dawn. Having fought under Uther the Lightbringer and Alexandros Mograine during the Third War, he now commands the defense of Light's Hope Chapel and directs the coalition's campaign to cleanse the Plaguelands.",al={"who is maxwell tyrosus","tyrosus lore","leader of argent dawn","argent dawn boss"}},{q="Why did Tyrosus leave the Scarlet Crusade?",a="Following the murder of Alexandros Mograine, the remnants of the Silver Hand in Lordaeron became increasingly radical and xenophobic, purging anyone who was not purely human. Tyrosus had always believed in cooperating with other races to defeat the Scourge, so he abandoned the zealots and joined the Argent Dawn.",al={"why did tyrosus leave scarlet crusade","tyrosus scarlet crusade","is tyrosus scarlet crusade"}},{q="Where can Maxwell Tyrosus be found?",a="He is located inside the sanctuary of Light's Hope Chapel, the Argent Dawn's fortified stronghold situated in the far eastern reaches of the Eastern Plaguelands.",al={"tyrosus location","where is maxwell tyrosus","tyrosus map"}},{q="What is Tyrosus's role in the war against Stratholme?",a="Tyrosus coordinates broad military strategy with Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff, tasking proven adventurers and strike teams to breach the fallen city of Stratholme and eliminate Baron Rivendare, the Lich King's commander in the region.",al={"tyrosus stratholme","tyrosus rivendare"}},{q="Does Tyrosus allow anyone to meet with him?",a="Tyrosus rarely grants audiences to outsiders, having spent years secluded in war councils directing the frontline effort. Adventurers must typically earn the deep respect of the Argent Dawn or present critical intelligence to gain his attention.",al={"can i talk to tyrosus","tyrosus audience"}},{q="What was Tyrosus's role in the Siege of the Sanguine?",a="During that battle, Tyrosus confronted Kirkessen the Zealous, a high-ranking lich serving the Lich King. Tyrosus struck a critical blow that permanently stripped Kirkessen of his physical body, preventing the undead sorcerer from ever manifesting in a corporeal form again.",al={"tyrosus kirkessen","siege of the sanguine"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Tyrosus represents the unbroken spirit of the Silver Hand, maintaining the virtues of compassion, unity, and discipline after Uther's death and the tragic corruption of the order's splinter factions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though born a nobleman of Lordaeron and a hero of the Alliance, Tyrosus now commits his forces to an independent order that welcomes anyone willing to fight the Scourge.",["faction:Horde"]="Unlike the zealots in Hearthglen and the Scarlet Monastery, Tyrosus has long championed cooperation with non-humans, ensuring Horde warriors and shamans are accepted as equals within Light's Hope Chapel."},kw={"argent dawn","kirkessen","light's hope chapel","paladin","scourge","silver hand","stratholme","tyrosus"},rel={"subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","topic:argent-dawn","zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:stratholme","npc:darion-mograine","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:scourge","npc:tirion-fordring"},src={"Lord Maxwell Tyrosus"}}
E["npc:nathanos-blightcaller"] = {t="npc",n="Nathanos Blightcaller",z="easternplaguelands",s="Nathanos Blightcaller, once Nathanos Marris, stands at his ruined homestead in the Eastern Plaguelands as the deadly champion of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner. In life he was the first and only human Ranger Lord of Quel'Thalas, and in undeath he trains Forsaken hunters while guarding the eastern frontier with biting contempt for all who approach.",h="Nathanos Blightcaller, once Nathanos Marris, stands at his ruined homestead in the Eastern Plaguelands as the...",sec={{t="The Only Human Farstrider",b="Before the Third War, Nathanos Marris was an extraordinary marksman and tactical genius hailing from the rural outskirts of Lordaeron. His battlefield exploits against the Amani trolls caught the attention of Sylvanas Windrunner, the Ranger-General of Silvermoon. Defying the staunch prejudices of elven nobility—including protests from Prince Kael'thas Sunstrider—Sylvanas elevated him into the Farstriders. Nathanos became the only human to ever attain the prestigious rank of Ranger Lord. Weary of elven court politics and cold sneers from peers like Lor'themar Theron, he spent his downtime at his family estate, the Marris Stead, where Sylvanas frequently visited him.",sp=0},{t="The Fall and Rebirth",b="When Prince Arthas and the Scourge swept through Lordaeron following the purge of Stratholme, the plague consumed the kingdom. Nathanos made a desperate stand at his estate, but fell to the monstrous abomination Ramstein the Gorger. Raised as a mindless undead thrall, he roamed the blighted fields killing in the Lich King's name. After Sylvanas shattered the Scourge's mental grip and established the Forsaken in the Undercity, she tracked him down. Her dark rangers subdued the rabid ghoul, and Sylvanas personally tore his consciousness free from the Lich King's will, returning his tactical brilliance and fiery loyalty to her side.",sp=0},{t="Champion of the Banshee Queen",b="Adopting the epithet Blightcaller, Nathanos took up permanent residence at the decrepit Marris Stead. He serves as Sylvanas's champion, hunter trainer, and regional spymaster in the contested Eastern Plaguelands, protected by foul plaguehounds. Alliance intelligence has identified his survival with deep alarm; Highlord Bolvar Fordragon views a master tactician of Nathanos's caliber leading undead forces as an intolerable threat to human survival, dispatching strike forces to assassinate the fallen Ranger Lord.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Nathanos Blightcaller?",a="Nathanos Blightcaller was Nathanos Marris, a renowned human marksman and the only non-elf ever appointed Ranger Lord of Quel'Thalas by Sylvanas Windrunner. Following his death and resurrection during the Third War, Sylvanas freed his mind from the Scourge. He now serves as her champion and hunter trainer at his ancestral home in the Eastern Plaguelands.",al={"who is nathanos","nathanos lore","who is the guy at marris stead"}},{q="Why is Nathanos at the Marris Stead?",a="The Marris Stead was Nathanos's childhood home in life. He preferred its quiet isolation to the snobbish politics of Silvermoon City. In undeath, he chose to return to his ruined estate, transforming it into an outpost to train Forsaken hunters and monitor Alliance and Scourge movements.",al={"where is nathanos","why is nathanos in plaguelands","marris stead nathanos"}},{q="How did Nathanos become an undead?",a="Nathanos was killed at his homestead during the Third War by the Scourge abomination Ramstein the Gorger. He rose as an obedient, mindless thrall to the Lich King until Sylvanas tracked him down, subdued him, and liberated his mind so he could join the Forsaken.",al={"how did nathanos die","who killed nathanos","nathanos death"}},{q="Why does the Alliance want to kill him?",a="Alliance leadership in Stormwind discovered that Nathanos Marris—one of the Alliance's greatest military minds and tactical geniuses—did not perish permanently, but instead joined the Forsaken. Viewing his tactical brilliance as an immense danger, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon orders his elimination.",al={"why kill nathanos","alliance quest nathanos","order must be restored"}},{q="What is his relationship with Sylvanas?",a="Nathanos was Sylvanas's prize pupil, trusted confidant, and champion. Sylvanas defied high elven tradition and her own prince to grant him the title of Ranger Lord, sparking widespread rumors of a romantic bond. In undeath, his loyalty to the Banshee Queen remains absolute and unwavering.",al={"sylvanas and nathanos","did sylvanas love nathanos","nathanos sylvanas romance"}},{q="Who are the hounds standing near him?",a="They are vicious plaguehounds that Nathanos trained himself. Kept at his side to guard the ruins of the Marris Stead, they attack any intruders foolish enough to trespass on his territory.",al={"nathanos dogs","marris stead hounds","blightcaller pets"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Nathanos is the highest-ranking hunter trainer for the Forsaken, bringing the rigorous, legendary Farstrider marksmanship techniques of Quel'Thalas to the undead of Lordaeron.",["race:Undead"]="As the champion of the Dark Lady, Nathanos embodies the bitter resilience of the Forsaken, though he has little patience for incompetence among his peers.",["faction:Alliance"]="Seeing a decorated hero of Lordaeron and a celebrated Farstrider fighting beneath the banner of the Forsaken is a stinging insult and a lethal tactical problem for Stormwind.",["faction:Horde"]="Nathanos provides critical tactical guidance and hunter training for the Horde in the Plaguelands, though he treats visitors with caustic disdain."},kw={"blightcaller","farstrider","hunter trainer","marris","marris stead","nathanos","plaguelands","sylvanas"},rel={"subzone:marris-stead","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:forsaken","npc:lor-themar-theron","topic:scourge","subzone:stratholme","zone:undercity"},src={"Nathanos Blightcaller"}}
E["subzone:blackwood-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackwood Lake",z="easternplaguelands",s="Blackwood Lake is a blighted body of water situated in the southern Eastern Plaguelands, teeming with hostile, corrupted elementals. Once the site of a peaceful Lordaeron village, the area is now haunted by memories of tragedy and war, watched over by a small frontline camp of the Argent Dawn.",h="Blackwood Lake is a blighted body of water situated in the southern Eastern Plaguelands, teeming with...",sec={{t="A Polluted Memory",b="Before the Third War, a quiet settlement named Blackwood rested along these shores. It was the ancestral home of Grand Marshal Othmar Garithos, whose family holdings and subjects were slaughtered during the Second War while he defended Quel'Thalas. Today, the town is utterly gone, and the lake itself has been poisoned by the rampant plague of undeath. Diseased and foul water elementals churn beneath the murky surface, attacking anyone who ventures near the shoreline.",sp=0},{t="Relics of the Fallen",b="The lake also holds grim relics from the Battle of Darrowshire. Local historical accounts, such as the Extended Annals of Darrowshire, record that the severed skull of the Scourge warlord Horgus the Ravager was cast into Blackwood Lake's rancid depths. Nearby, an Argent Dawn medic tends to battered infantry at a small forward outpost, struggling to keep soldiers alive in the shadow of the Scourge's devastation.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What creatures lurk in Blackwood Lake?",a="The lake is infested with corrupted water elementals. Like much of the freshwater in the Plaguelands, the waters have been twisted by necromantic runoff and filth, warping the local spirits into violent, toxic entities.",al={"what is in the water","lake monsters","elementals in blackwood lake"}},{q="What town used to stand here?",a="A Lordaeron village called Blackwood once stood on these shores. It was ruled by the family of Grand Marshal Othmar Garithos before it was sacked and destroyed by an orcish raiding party during the Second War.",al={"blackwood town","who lived here","garithos hometown"}},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn stationed at the lake?",a="The Argent Dawn maintains a small field camp near the lake where an Argent Medic cares for wounded infantry. It acts as an emergency station for patrols fighting along the roads between Darrowshire and nearby Scourge strongholds.",al={"argent camp","argent medic","why are there soldiers here"}},{q="What Darrowshire relic is buried in Blackwood Lake?",a="According to the Annals of Darrowshire, the skull of Horgus the Ravager, one of the primary Scourge leaders during the assault on Darrowshire, was hurled into the lake's depths after he was brought down.",al={"horgus the ravager head","quest item in lake","annals of darrowshire lake"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Lordaeron, Blackwood Lake is a bitter reminder of the fall of Grand Marshal Garithos's line and the sheer totality with which the Scourge erased the kingdom's rural townships.",["class:Paladin"]="The polluted waters and decaying atmosphere around Blackwood Lake are a stark display of the blight corrupting Lordaeron's natural elementals, demanding the purifying touch of the Light."},kw={"blackwood","darrowshire","elementals","garithos","horgus","lake","plaguelands"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:darrowshire","topic:argent-dawn"},src={"Blackwood Lake"}}
E["subzone:browman-mill"] = {t="subzone",n="Browman Mill",z="easternplaguelands",s="Browman Mill is a blighted lumber mill situated just north of Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands. Once a thriving piece of Lordaeron's timber trade, it now swarms with undead minions under the iron grip of the Scourge. Its former proprietor, Stephen Browman, remains trapped in death within his ruined workshop.",h="Browman Mill is a blighted lumber mill situated just north of Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Ruined Industry",b="Before the Third War, Browman Mill served the surrounding towns and homesteads of Lordaeron, processing lumber harvested from the rich forests of the Eastweald. When the Scourge plague rolled across the kingdom, the mill fell alongside the rest of the province. Today, rotting timbers and shattered wheels sit idle while abominations, banshees, and skeletal warriors patrol the perimeter. Its close proximity to Light's Hope Chapel makes it a constant and menacing reminder of the undead horde pressing against the Argent Dawn's doorstep.",sp=0},{t="The Overseer's Fate",b="The mill's original owner, Stephen Browman, met the same grim fate as countless commoners of Lordaeron. Murdered when the Scourge overran the estate, he was raised into undeath as a ravenous ghoul. Stripped of his humanity and enslaved to the Lich King's will, Browman lingers within the dark confines of his former mill, guarding the splintered ruins of his life's work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Browman Mill located?",a="Browman Mill is located in the far eastern stretch of the Eastern Plaguelands, sitting directly north of Light's Hope Chapel.",al={"browman mill location","where is browman mill","how to find browman mill"}},{q="What kind of enemies inhabit the mill?",a="The grounds are infested with Scourge forces, including hulking abominations, wailing banshees, skeletal fiends, and wandering ghouls.",al={"browman mill mobs","who is at browman mill","what lives at browman mill"}},{q="Who was Stephen Browman?",a="Stephen Browman was the original human owner and operator of the lumber mill. He was slaughtered during the fall of Lordaeron and reanimated as an undead ghoul, bound to guard his ruined building.",al={"who is stephen browman","stephen browman lore","browman ghoul"}},{q="Why is Browman Mill dangerous to travelers?",a="Its heavy concentration of powerful undead makes it a lethal hazard, particularly because it sits just a short ride north of the Argent Dawn stronghold at Light's Hope Chapel.",al={"why is browman mill dangerous","threat of browman mill"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The desecrated remains of the mill and the tormented spirits haunting its grounds represent everything the holy orders fight to cleanse from Lordaeron.",["race:Undead"]="Stephen Browman's enslavement is a stark reminder of the fate shared by all victims of the Lich King who were denied the free will won by the Forsaken."},kw={"abominations","banshees","browman mill","eastern plaguelands","light's hope chapel","lumber mill","scourge","stephen browman"},rel={"subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:light"},src={"Browman Mill"}}
E["subzone:corin-s-crossing"] = {t="subzone",n="Corin's Crossing",z="easternplaguelands",s="Corin's Crossing is a ruined human settlement situated at a major crossroads in south-central Eastern Plaguelands. Once a thriving waystation between Stratholme, Tyr's Hand, Darrowshire, and Andorhal, the devastated town is now utterly overrun by the Scourge. Its crumbling town hall and forge harbor lingering horrors, including invisible spectral watchers.",h="Corin's Crossing is a ruined human settlement situated at a major crossroads in south-central Eastern...",sec={{t="A Shattered Crossroads",b="Before the Third War, Corin's Crossing served as a central junction for travel across eastern Lordaeron. Positioned between the shimmering waters of Lake Mereldar and what has now become the blighted chasm of the Infectis Scar, its thoroughfares once bore merchants, couriers, and pilgrims traveling between the great bastion of Stratholme and the southern strongholds. When the plague swept through the province, the settlement stood directly in the path of destruction, collapsing swiftly beneath the sheer weight of the undead vanguard.",sp=0},{t="A Haven of the Damned",b="Today, Corin's Crossing is thoroughly lost to the Scourge. Wandering undead pack the muddy streets, while rotting hulks and ghouls linger inside the hollowed-out blacksmith shop and town hall. The town is notably treacherous for scouts: spectral Unseen Servants drift among the ruins completely invisible to ordinary eyes, piercing mundane stealth and ambushing anyone attempting to slip past the main horde undetected.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Corin's Crossing before the plague?",a="It was a prosperous hub town in eastern Lordaeron. Centered around a town hall and blacksmith forge, it served travelers moving between Stratholme, Tyr's Hand, Darrowshire, and Andorhal before the Scourge wiped out its populace.",al={"corins crossing history","corins crossing lore","what was corins crossing"}},{q="Why is Corin's Crossing so hazardous for stealthy travelers?",a="The town is haunted by Unseen Servants—invisible phantoms bound to the Scourge. These specters can pierce magical and mundane stealth effortlessly, catching unwary rogues or scouts by surprise and alerting nearby undead.",al={"stealth in corins crossing","unseen servants","rogue corins crossing"}},{q="What major landmarks surround the town?",a="Corin's Crossing sits directly in the south-central Eastern Plaguelands. The blighted trench of the Infectis Scar lies immediately nearby, Lake Mereldar rests along its border, and the Argent Dawn outpost at Light's Shield Tower stands just to the north.",al={"corins crossing location","where is corins crossing"}},{q="Who controls Corin's Crossing today?",a="The Scourge holds total dominion over the ruins. No living defenders remain within the town, and the entire settlement swarms with wandering undead soldiers and spirits.",al={"who owns corins crossing","corins crossing faction"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Do not trust your shadows here. Unseen Servants roam the alleys invisible to mortal sight and see right through your stealth, making a casual walk through the town square fatal.",["class:Paladin"]="The ruins of Corin's Crossing represent the utter desecration of Lordaeron's heartland, lingering as a wretched Scourge stronghold that mocks the holy bastion of Stratholme further up the road."},kw={"corin's crossing","corins crossing","eastern plaguelands","infectis scar","lake mereldar","light's shield tower","unseen servants"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:infectis-scar","subzone:lake-mereldar","subzone:stratholme","subzone:tyr-s-hand","subzone:darrowshire","topic:scourge"},src={"Corin's Crossing"}}
E["subzone:crown-guard-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Crown Guard Tower",z="easternplaguelands",s="Crown Guard Tower is a ruined Lordaeron scout tower situated in the southern Eastern Plaguelands. Sacked during the Third War by the Scourge, its strategic vantage point makes it an actively contested fortification between Alliance and Horde forces venturing through the blighted lands.",h="Crown Guard Tower is a ruined Lordaeron scout tower situated in the southern Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Fallen Bulwark",b="Once part of the Kingdom of Lordaeron's defensive network, Crown Guard Tower fell swiftly during the Scourge onslaught and was reduced to charred stone. Despite the surrounding desolation and constant undead presence, its elevated platform remains a vital observation post overlooking the southern roads of the Plaguelands. As both the Alliance and Horde attempt to establish permanent footholds in the region to oppose the Lich King's armies, the tower serves as an active frontline skirmish site where both factions repeatedly clash to secure supply routes and tactical supremacy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Crown Guard Tower originally built for?",a="It served as a regional military watchtower and scout outpost for the human Kingdom of Lordaeron before the Third War, guarding the roads against incursions.",al={"crown guard tower history","why was it built","lordaeron tower"}},{q="Why is the tower ruined?",a="The tower was destroyed during the Scourge invasion of Lordaeron, when waves of undead overran the kingdom's defenses and left the structure in rubble.",al={"who destroyed crown guard tower","what happened here"}},{q="Why do the Alliance and Horde fight over it?",a="Controlling the fallen tower allows either faction to fortify their local presence, secure the nearby roadways, and reinforce offensive operations in the Eastern Plaguelands.",al={"why fight for the tower","pvp tower","strategic value"}},{q="Is the tower permanently held by any faction?",a="No. Control continually shifts as Alliance and Horde warbands assault and reclaim the beacon, neither side yet maintaining an enduring occupation.",al={"who owns the tower","who controls crown guard tower"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, reclaiming Crown Guard Tower is an effort to restore order to Lordaeron's ancestral soil and deny Horde scouts an overwatch on key transport lanes.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde targets the tower to anchor their logistics across the Plaguelands and counter Alliance encroachments east of the river."},kw={"crown guard tower","eastern plaguelands","lordaeron","scourge","scout tower","watchtower"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:horde","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel"},src={"Crown Guard Tower"}}
E["subzone:crypt-light-s-hope-chapel"] = {t="subzone",n="Crypt (Light's Hope Chapel)",z="easternplaguelands",s="Tucked away behind Light's Hope Chapel sits a stone crypt nestled among the graves of the chapel's sprawling cemetery. It serves as an austere tomb on consecrated grounds where the Argent Dawn honors fallen champions and conducts trials of faith against lingering remnants of darkness.",h="Tucked away behind Light's Hope Chapel sits a stone crypt nestled among the graves of the chapel's sprawling...",sec={{t="A Tomb in Consecrated Earth",b="Behind the fortified sanctuary of Light's Hope Chapel stretches a somber graveyard, housing the remains of defenders who perished against the Scourge in the Plaguelands. Dominating this burial ground is the stone crypt, built to inter honored souls under the vigil of the Argent Dawn. Even in a sanctuary consecrated to the Holy Light, the underground confines of the crypt remain cold and shadow-strewn, requiring constant vigilance to ensure unhallowed spirits or lingering dark magic do not take root.",sp=0},{t="The Trial of the Crypt",b="The Argent Dawn does not merely treat the crypt as a monument, but as a crucible for proven crusaders. Initiates and champions who answer the Argent Dawn's summons are directed to test their mettle in this underground chamber. Through ritual trials, the spectral form of Lord Raymond George can be summoned forth within the tomb, challenging defenders of the Light to prove their devotion and combat prowess against restless manifestations of the past.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is this crypt located?",a="The crypt is situated directly behind Light's Hope Chapel in the eastern reaches of the Eastern Plaguelands, nestled within the large cemetery grounds.",al={"crypt location","where is crypt lights hope","find the crypt"}},{q="Who is buried in the cemetery and crypt?",a="The graveyard and crypt house soldiers, paladins, and priests who fell defending Lordaeron and fighting the Scourge, preserved on holy ground by the Argent Dawn.",al={"who is in the crypt","cemetery dead","who is buried here"}},{q="Who is Lord Raymond George?",a="Lord Raymond George is a fallen champion whose spirit can be summoned within the crypt by seasoned adventurers undertaking trials of strength and conviction for the Argent Dawn.",al={"raymond george","lord raymond george lore","summon crypt boss"}},{q="Is the crypt safe from the Scourge?",a="While the surrounding chapel grounds are profoundly blessed, the deep underground chambers of the crypt are cold and less touched by radiant Light, requiring constant watching by the Argent Dawn against corruption.",al={"is the crypt holy","can scourge enter crypt","crypt holy ground"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Standing before the crypt is a solemn reminder of the crusaders who preceded you, offering a place to reflect on sacrifice and the eternal duty to protect Lordaeron's dead.",["class:Priest"]="The crypt provides an altar of quiet contemplation on holy ground, where prayers for the fallen shield their resting places from shadow."},kw={"argent dawn","cemetery","crypt","eastern plaguelands","graveyard","light's hope chapel","lord raymond george"},rel={"subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:light"},src={"Crypt (Light's Hope Chapel)"}}
E["subzone:darrowshire"] = {t="subzone",n="Darrowshire",z="easternplaguelands",s="Darrowshire is a ruined village in the southern hills of the Eastern Plaguelands, once a peaceful hamlet of Lordaeron. During the Third War, its residents mounted a desperate, tragic stand against an overwhelming Scourge force. Today, only shattered timbers, restless spirits, and bitter memories linger amid the silence.",h="Darrowshire is a ruined village in the southern hills of the Eastern Plaguelands, once a peaceful hamlet of...",sec={{t="A Tragic Stand",b="Before the plague consumed northern Lordaeron, Darrowshire was a humble rural settlement nestled beneath the southern cliffs. When the Scourge marched south during the Third War, a force led by the death knight Marduk Blackpool and the ghoul lord Horgus the Ravager besieged the town. The villagers and local defenders fought valiantly, momentarily holding the line against impossible odds. Ultimately, the defense collapsed, and the town was slaughtered down to the last soul. Rather than finding peace in death, many of Darrowshire's fallen defenders were reanimated as ghouls to bolster the Scourge's ranks, leaving the village an eerie, empty memorial of lost valor.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Battle",b="Though long abandoned by the living, Darrowshire is far from completely empty. The psychic weight of the slaughter clings heavily to the valley, trapping spectral remnants of the townspeople within the ruins. Travelers passing through report strange phenomena, including chilling reenactments where the tragic battle unfolds again in ghostly silence. The ground remains saturated with sorrow, serving as a bleak reminder of what the Scourge tore away from the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to Darrowshire?",a="Darrowshire was destroyed during the Third War when a massive Scourge army assaulted the town. Led by the death knight Marduk Blackpool and the ghoul lord Horgus the Ravager, the undead overwhelmed the town's defenders and slaughtered the inhabitants, leaving the settlement in ruins.",al={"darrowshire history","why is darrowshire destroyed","what happened here"}},{q="Who were the leaders of the Scourge attack on Darrowshire?",a="The assault was led by the death knight Marduk Blackpool alongside Horgus the Ravager, a monstrous ghoul lord. Together, their forces broke the village's defenders and doomed the settlement.",al={"who attacked darrowshire","darrowshire villains","horgus and marduk"}},{q="Why is Darrowshire haunted?",a="The slaughter was so sudden and horrific that the spirits of the fallen remained bound to the earth. In addition to ghostly apparitions lingering in the ruined buildings, the brutal battle itself is said to periodically replay in spectral form, trapping the dead in their final, tragic moments.",al={"darrowshire ghosts","why are there spirits in darrowshire"}},{q="What became of the villagers who died defending the town?",a="Most of the defenders were butchered where they stood, and many of their corpses were reanimated by necromancers into mindless ghouls, forced to serve the very Scourge army that destroyed their homes.",al={"darrowshire villagers","defenders of darrowshire"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of the Alliance, Darrowshire is a solemn testament to the sheer devastation inflicted upon Lordaeron, where ordinary folk made a hopeless stand to defend their families.",["class:Paladin"]="The tragic fate of Darrowshire stands as an enduring call for paladins to bring the purifying Light to the Plaguelands, both to strike down the undead and lay tortured spirits to rest."},kw={"battle of darrowshire","darrowshire","eastern plaguelands","ghouls","horgus the ravager","lordaeron","marduk blackpool"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:third-war","topic:light","npc:nathanos-blightcaller"},src={"Darrowshire"}}
E["subzone:death-cultist-base-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Death Cultist Base Camp",z="easternplaguelands",s="In the year 25 ADP, this location west of Tyr's Hand is known as the Scarlet Base Camp, an armed enclave of the Scarlet Crusade overlooking the road into their southeastern fortress. Travelers here will find zealots of the crusade guarding the blighted hills.",h="In the year 25 ADP, this location west of Tyr's Hand is known as the Scarlet Base Camp, an armed enclave of...",sec={{t="A Crusader Staging Ground",b="Occupying high ground along the winding path toward Tyr's Hand, this outpost serves the Scarlet Crusade as an advanced guard post in the southeastern Eastern Plaguelands. From here, crusaders mount watches against both wandering undead and interloping travelers traveling along the blighted trails. While Scourge necromancers covet the territory for their dark arts, the camp remains firmly in the clutches of Scarlet zealots who answer any trespass with righteous steel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this area called Death Cultist Base Camp?",a="In 25 ADP this encampment is known as the Scarlet Base Camp, not a death cultist camp. It serves as an outer defensive position for the Scarlet Crusade guarding the approach to Tyr's Hand.",al={"why death cultist","cultist camp name","isn't this scarlet camp"}},{q="Who controls this encampment right now?",a="The camp is manned by soldiers of the Scarlet Crusade. They treat all outsiders—both the mindless Scourge and living travelers of the Alliance or Horde—as tainted enemies.",al={"who is here","who controls the camp","scarlet or scourge"}},{q="Where is this camp located?",a="It sits nestled in the hills of the southeastern Eastern Plaguelands, positioned directly west of the grand scarlet bastion of Tyr's Hand.",al={"where is it","camp location","where is scarlet base camp"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The camp stands as a sobering reminder of how far the Scarlet Crusade has fallen, twisting the righteous light into paranoid zealotry against all outside their ranks."},kw={"death cultist base camp","eastern plaguelands","plague cauldron","scarlet base camp","scarlet crusade","scourge","tyr's hand"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-base-camp","subzone:tyr-s-hand","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scourge","subzone:cauldron"},src={"Death Cultist Base Camp"}}
E["subzone:death-s-step"] = {t="subzone",n="Death's Step",z="easternplaguelands",s="Death's Step is a blighted, tree-lined hollow tucked along the southern border of the Eastern Plaguelands near the shores of Darrowmere Lake. Hemmed in just west of the Undercroft, it crawls with vile Scourge creations and purveyors of disease.",h="Death's Step is a blighted, tree-lined hollow tucked along the southern border of the Eastern Plaguelands...",sec={{t="A Foul Hollow",b="Tucked away near the northern water's edge of Darrowmere Lake and situated directly west of the tomb grounds of the Undercroft, Death's Step is an ominous pocket of Scourge corruption. Enclosed by dead and weeping trees, the clearing is prowled by putrifiers and warped miscreations. While small compared to the massive blighted ruins nearby, it serves as an unwelcome ambush point for anyone navigating the lake's banks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Death's Step located?",a="Death's Step lies in the southern reach of the Eastern Plaguelands, right along the northern shore of Darrowmere Lake and directly west of the Undercroft.",al={"deaths step location","where is deaths step"}},{q="What creatures inhabit Death's Step?",a="The clearing is occupied by Scourge horrors, notably putrifiers and grotesque miscreations that wander among the diseased trees in small packs.",al={"deaths step mobs","what is in deaths step","enemies deaths step"}},{q="Why is this area significant to travelers?",a="Aside from its perilous proximity to the crypts of the Undercroft and the banks of Darrowmere Lake, it is a treacherous natural choke point where the Scourge festers unchecked away from the main roads.",al={"why go to deaths step","deaths step significance"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The vile putrifiers and twisted miscreations brooding within this enclave are prime examples of the undead blight that Paladins are sworn to purge from Lordaeron."},kw={"darrowmere lake","death's step","deaths step","eastern plaguelands","miscreation","putrifier","scourge","undercroft"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:undercroft","subzone:darrowmere-lake"},src={"Death's Step"}}
E["subzone:eastwall-gate"] = {t="subzone",n="Eastwall Gate",z="easternplaguelands",s="Eastwall Gate is a fortified side entrance set into the perimeter wall of the fallen city of Stratholme. Located in the northern reaches of the Eastern Plaguelands, it offers a direct secondary access point into Stratholme's interior ruins, bypassing the chaos of the city's main gates.",h="Eastwall Gate is a fortified side entrance set into the perimeter wall of the fallen city of Stratholme.",sec={{t="The Back Door to Ruin",b="While the grand main entrance of Stratholme opens directly onto King's Square, the Eastwall Gate pierces the city's eastern fortifications. Barred securely against intruders, this gateway leads straight into Elders' Square, close by the steps of Alonsus Chapel. For those venturing into the burning heart of the Scourge stronghold, bypassing the front barricades can mean the difference between a swift strike into the city's depths and a meatgrinder assault through the forward undead lines.",sp=0},{t="Through the Iron Lattice",b="Gaining entry through the Eastwall Gate is no simple matter. It is sealed tightly by heavy ironwork that requires the Key to the City, recovered from inside Stratholme itself, or an exceptionally skilled infiltrator capable of picking masterwork locks. Once past the threshold, a heavy mechanical lever mounted on the inner wall allows travelers to raise the portcullis from the inside, opening a reliable path for allies to follow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Eastwall Gate lead?",a="The gate opens into Elders' Square within the ruined city of Stratholme. It stands in close proximity to the historic Alonsus Chapel.",al={"where does eastwall gate go","eastwall gate destination","what is behind eastwall gate"}},{q="How can the gate be opened?",a="The Eastwall Gate is firmly locked. It can be opened using the Key to the City found within Stratholme, or picked by an expert rogue who has mastered lockpicking. Once inside, an inner lever can raise the gate manually.",al={"how to open eastwall gate","unlock eastwall gate","eastwall gate key"}},{q="Why would adventurers use this entrance over the main gate?",a="Entering through the Eastwall Gate allows strike teams to bypass the heavily infested front streets and begin their assault directly near Elders' Square, providing quicker access to specific quarters of the city.",al={"why use eastwall gate","side entrance benefits","why side gate stratholme"}},{q="Can you open the gate from the inside?",a="Yes. A lever located on the inner Stratholme side of the gate allows anyone inside to lift the gate and let others through without using a key.",al={"lever inside eastwall gate","open eastwall gate from inside"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="The sturdy lock of the Eastwall Gate demands the absolute pinnacle of lockpicking skill, making a master rogue invaluable for bypassing the front entrance without the Key to the City.",["class:Paladin"]="Passing through the Eastwall Gate puts crusaders immediately near Alonsus Chapel, a holy sanctuary now surrounded by the ashes and horrors of the Scourge."},kw={"alonsus chapel","eastern plaguelands","eastwall gate","elders' square","key to the city","portcullis","side entrance","stratholme"},rel={"subzone:stratholme","zone:easternplaguelands"},src={"Eastwall Gate"}}
E["subzone:eastwall-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Eastwall Tower",z="easternplaguelands",s="Eastwall Tower is a ruined Lordaeron scout tower situated in the Eastern Plaguelands near the eastern road. Sacked during the Third War when the Scourge swept across the kingdom, its remains now serve as a vital vantage point fought over by Alliance and Horde forces seeking a foothold in the infected wilderness.",h="Eastwall Tower is a ruined Lordaeron scout tower situated in the Eastern Plaguelands near the eastern road.",sec={{t="A Ruined Watch on the Border",b="Built as a border sentinel for the kingdom of Lordaeron, Eastwall Tower once watched over travelers heading toward the far reaches of the realm. When the Scourge invaded during the Third War, the outpost was crushed along with the surrounding settlements, leaving shattered stone arches and burnt timber behind. Now, with the Lich King's armies still infesting the region, the tower's elevated position makes it an indispensable forward post. Vanguard scouts from both the Alliance and the Horde clash violently over its ramparts, seeking to secure supply lines and bolster regional control against the surrounding horrors.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Eastwall Tower before it fell?",a="Eastwall Tower was originally a defensive scout tower constructed by the Kingdom of Lordaeron. It formed part of the regional border watch network, safeguarding trade routes and outlying farms before the Third War brought about Lordaeron's fall.",al={"eastwall tower history","who built eastwall tower","what was this place"}},{q="Who destroyed the tower?",a="The tower was destroyed by the Scourge during Prince Arthas Menethil's conquest and the subsequent undead ravaging of Lordaeron. Undead monstrosities smashed its defenses, leaving the defenders dead and the structure in ruins.",al={"how was eastwall tower ruined","what happened to eastwall tower"}},{q="Why are the Alliance and Horde fighting over these ruins?",a="Even in ruins, the tower commands high ground along the eastern roadways of the Plaguelands. Both factions seek to fortify their forward positions, protect supply lines, and establish staging grounds against the Scourge without ceding territory to their mortal rivals.",al={"why fight here","pvp tower lore","why is eastwall tower contested"}},{q="Is the tower safe to rest at?",a="The tower is actively contested and never truly secure. Whichever faction currently holds the beacon may station sentries there, but wild Scourge forces roam close by and rival champions frequently launch skirmishes to seize control.",al={"can i rest here","friendly guards"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, retaking Eastwall Tower honors the fallen soldiers of Lordaeron and secures the approach to Light's Hope Chapel against Scourge and Horde incursions alike.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing Eastwall Tower establishes a vital forward outpost in contested northern lands, ensuring Horde forces are not trapped or cut off by Alliance expeditions."},kw={"eastern plaguelands","eastwall tower","lordaeron","plaguelands tower","pvp tower","scout tower"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Eastwall Tower"}}
E["subzone:fungal-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Fungal Vale",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Fungal Vale is a deeply blighted depression located in the south-central Eastern Plaguelands, just north of the Crown Guard Tower and Marris Stead. Choked in a murky haze and blanketed with dark purple earth, the valley showcases the raw, mutating power of the Plague of Undeath. It swarms with roaming Scourge horrors and mortal acolytes serving the Cult of the Damned.",h="The Fungal Vale is a deeply blighted depression located in the south-central Eastern Plaguelands, just north...",sec={{t="A Garden of Rot",b="Situated north of Marris Stead, the Fungal Vale represents one of the most thoroughly corrupted pockets in Lordaeron. The ground here has turned a sickly purple, swollen with alien fungal growths and drowning under a perpetual, murky haze produced by necrotic spores. Rather than simply killing the ecosystem, the Plague of Undeath has warped the soil to cultivate unholy flora, feeding monstrous carrion beasts and shambling undead. Cult of the Damned members frequent the area, tending to the blighted blooms and conducting foul rites amidst the unnatural decay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Fungal Vale?",a="It is a corrupted valley in the southern reach of the Eastern Plaguelands, lying directly north of Crown Guard Tower and Marris Stead. The area is heavily contaminated by the Plague of Undeath, transforming normal vegetation into overgrown fungal blight.",al={"where is fungal vale","fungal vale lore","fungal vale overview"}},{q="Why is the ground purple here?",a="The soil has been thoroughly saturated by the Plague of Undeath. Rather than letting plant life completely perish, the necrotic contamination mutates the land into a fertile bed for virulent spores, turning the earth a bruised purple.",al={"why is the ground purple","purple dirt plaguelands","fungal vale ground"}},{q="Who controls this area?",a="The Fungal Vale is held by the Scourge and mortal cultists of the Cult of the Damned. Undead horrors wander the haze alongside acolytes who nurture the corrupted fungal ecology.",al={"who is in fungal vale","fungal vale enemies","cultists fungal vale"}},{q="Where is it located relative to local landmarks?",a="It lies in south-central Eastern Plaguelands, positioned directly north of the road between Marris Stead and the Crown Guard Tower.",al={"how to get to fungal vale","fungal vale location","near crown guard tower"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The Fungal Vale represents the ultimate mockery of natural life, where nature's cycle has been replaced by perpetual, unholy rot driven by the Scourge.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The blighted, fungal-choked ground stands as a stark warning of what necromancy does to the native flora of Lordaeron."},kw={"blight","crown guard tower","cult of the damned","eastern plaguelands","fungal vale","fungus","marris stead","plague of undeath","scourge"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:crown-guard-tower","subzone:marris-stead","topic:cult-of-the-damned","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:scourge"},src={"Fungal Vale"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-arms-tyr-s-hand"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Arms (Tyr's Hand)",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Hall of Arms is a heavily guarded wing within Tyr's Hand Abbey in southeastern Eastern Plaguelands. It serves as a staging ground and barracks for the martial vanguard of the Scarlet Crusade garrisoned at the stronghold. Positioned across the abbey from the library, it houses some of the crusade's most zealous and well-armored fighters.",h="The Hall of Arms is a heavily guarded wing within Tyr's Hand Abbey in southeastern Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Bastion of Steel",b="Situated to the south of the abbey's main hall, the Hall of Arms functions as an armory and quarters for the militant forces of Tyr's Hand. While the opposing wing holds archives and holy texts, this wing is dedicated purely to the discipline of war. Clad in heavy armor and sworn to eradicate the undead and anyone deemed impure, the Scarlet defenders stationed here maintain a tireless watch over their eastern bastion, keeping weapons sharpened and shields polished against the surrounding horrors of the Plaguelands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Hall of Arms located?",a="The Hall of Arms is located within Tyr's Hand Abbey, the grand cathedral fortress situated inside Tyr's Hand in the southeastern corner of the Eastern Plaguelands. It forms the southern wing of the abbey complex, opposite the Library Wing.",al={"hall of arms location","where is hall of arms","tyrs hand abbey hall of arms"}},{q="Who occupies the Hall of Arms?",a="The wing is held exclusively by elite martial forces of the Scarlet Crusade. Seasoned warriors, paladins, and guards assemble here, maintaining armaments and preparing for battle against the Scourge and any outsiders entering their sanctuary.",al={"who lives in hall of arms","hall of arms enemies","scarlet crusade hall of arms"}},{q="What is the purpose of this wing compared to the rest of the abbey?",a="While the abbey's opposite wing focuses on study, contemplation, and scriptures, the Hall of Arms is built specifically for physical defense, troop housing, and weaponry upkeep. It ensures that the holy bastion remains militarily formidable against Scourge incursions.",al={"purpose of hall of arms","what is hall of arms for"}},{q="Can members of the Alliance enter peacefully?",a="No. Despite sharing human roots and venerating the Holy Light, the Scarlet Crusade in Tyr's Hand is completely fanatical. They view all outsiders as potential carriers of the plague or sympathizers with evil, attacking both Alliance and Horde travelers on sight.",al={"is scarlet crusade friendly to alliance","can alliance visit hall of arms","will tyrs hand attack me"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For knights of the Silver Hand, stepping into the Hall of Arms is a bitter sight, watching the sacred traditions of holy martial combat twisted into zealous isolationism.",["class:Warrior"]="The armaments and disciplined martial readying in the Hall of Arms represent peak human militarism, even if wielded in service of fanaticism."},kw={"abbey","armory","eastern plaguelands","hall of arms","scarlet crusade","tyr's hand","tyrs hand"},rel={"subzone:tyr-s-hand-abbey","subzone:tyr-s-hand","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:light"},src={"Hall of Arms (Tyr's Hand)"}}
E["subzone:infectis-scar"] = {t="subzone",n="Infectis Scar",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Infectis Scar is a deep, unnatural chasm carved into the blighted terrain of the Eastern Plaguelands near Corin's Crossing. Unlike natural ravines, this wound in the earth was ripped open by necromantic power when a cursed runeblade shattered against a dwarven shield. The blight festering at the bottom of the fissure remains an enduring testament to the Scourge's dark sorcery.",h="The Infectis Scar is a deep, unnatural chasm carved into the blighted terrain of the Eastern Plaguelands near...",sec={{t="A Wound of Dark Magic",b="While neighboring gorges like the Pestilent Scar originated as natural terrain features poisoned by the plague, the Infectis Scar is entirely artificial. It was created during the third war's violent clashes near Corin's Crossing. When the notorious death knight Marduk Blackpool clashed with a stalwart dwarf captain, Marduk's cursed runesword shattered against the captain's shield. Discarding the broken weapon, Marduk kept the hilt, but the severed runeblade sank deep into the soil. Its foul enchantment violently tore open the crust of the earth, creating the jagged chasm that sits festering in the Plaguelands today.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How was the Infectis Scar formed?",a="It was created during a battle near Corin's Crossing when the death knight Marduk Blackpool's runesword broke upon the shield of a dwarven captain. When the shattered blade hit the ground, its dark magic burrowed deep into the earth and tore open a massive rift.",al={"infectis scar origin","how did infectis scar happen","who made the infectis scar"}},{q="How is it different from the Pestilent Scar?",a="The Pestilent Scar was originally a natural gorge that was corrupted by the Scourge's plague. The Infectis Scar did not exist naturally; it was entirely blasted into existence by the malevolent sorcery leaking from Marduk Blackpool's broken runeblade.",al={"difference between infectis and pestilent scar","pestilent scar comparison"}},{q="Who was Marduk Blackpool?",a="Marduk Blackpool, known as the Black, was a death knight in service to the Scourge who participated in the slaughter across Lordaeron, including the assault on Darrowshire and skirmishes around Corin's Crossing.",al={"marduk blackpool","who is marduk"}},{q="Where is the sword now?",a="The blade of the shattered runesword sank deep into the bottom of the chasm it created, while Marduk Blackpool kept only the hilt with him after the clash.",al={"runeblade location","where is the blade"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The scar stands as a monument to dwarven resilience: it was carved only because an unnamed dwarf captain's shield held firm against a death knight's dark runeblade, shattering the cursed steel.",["class:Paladin"]="The chasm radiates the corrupting residue of necromantic sorcery, demonstrating how profoundly cursed runes can desecrate the earth when severed from their wielder."},kw={"chasm","corin's crossing","darrowshire","infectis scar","marduk blackpool","pestilent scar","runesword"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:corin-s-crossing","subzone:pestilent-scar","subzone:darrowshire","topic:dwarf"},src={"Infectis Scar"}}
E["subzone:lake-mereldar"] = {t="subzone",n="Lake Mereldar",z="easternplaguelands",s="Lake Mereldar is a sprawling, contaminated body of water resting south of Corin's Crossing in the Eastern Plaguelands. Once part of the idyllic rural heartland of Lordaeron, its corrupted waters now spawn twisted elementals and rot beneath the lingering taint of the Scourge.",h="Lake Mereldar is a sprawling, contaminated body of water resting south of Corin's Crossing in the Eastern...",sec={{t="A Polluted Haven",b="Situated just south of the crossroads town of Corin's Crossing, Lake Mereldar was once a peaceful fixture of northern Lordaeron's countryside. Dotting its shores are the decaying ruins of an old homestead, an abandoned shack, and a dilapidated ferry that once carried local farmers and travelers across the gentle waters. With the coming of the Scourge and the plague of undeath, the lake fell into complete ruin. The surrounding soil withered, and the waters turned foul and poisonous.",sp=0},{t="Twisted Inhabitants",b="The unnatural blight seeping into Lake Mereldar has thoroughly infected the local ecosystem and the spirits tied to it. Blighted Surges—corrupted water elementals driven mad by necromantic residue—lurk in the shallows and surface without warning. Along the weed-choked banks, vicious beasts such as Plague Ravagers prowl the mud, preying on whatever living creatures stray too close to the dead shoreline.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Lake Mereldar located?",a="Lake Mereldar sits in the central-southern expanse of the Eastern Plaguelands, directly south of the ruined town of Corin's Crossing.",al={"mereldar location","where is lake mereldar","find lake mereldar"}},{q="Why are there water elementals in the lake?",a="The water elementals here, known as Blighted Surges, have been twisted and driven hostile by the pervasive necromantic blight that seeped into the lake during the fall of Lordaeron.",al={"blighted surge","water elementals mereldar","corrupted elementals"}},{q="Who owned the shack and ferry on the shore?",a="They belonged to a local farming homestead established before the Third War. When the plague ravaged the Eastweald, the homesteaders perished or fled, leaving their house and ferry to rot.",al={"ferry ruins","mereldar house","abandoned dock"}},{q="Is the water safe to drink or swim in?",a="No. The lake is heavily fouled by the plague of undeath, making it hazardous to drink, swim in, or harvest from, and its waters harbor aggressive, blighted creatures.",al={"can you drink the water","is lake mereldar poisoned"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The existence of Blighted Surges in Lake Mereldar is a sobering testament to how the Scourge's foul magic corrupts even natural elemental spirits into mindless, violent horrors."},kw={"blighted surge","corin's crossing","eastern plaguelands","elementals","ferry","lake mereldar","plague ravager"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:corin-s-crossing"},src={"Lake Mereldar"}}
E["subzone:library-wing-tyr-s-hand"] = {t="subzone",n="Library Wing (Tyr's Hand)",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Library Wing is a secluded hall inside Tyr's Hand Abbey, nestled within the Scarlet Crusade's heavily fortified redoubt in the Eastern Plaguelands. Once dedicated to holy study and contemplation, its shelves are now consumed by the zealous order's rigid dogma and propaganda. Members of the Crusade congregate here to study scripture and guard the sanctum's religious relics.",h="The Library Wing is a secluded hall inside Tyr's Hand Abbey, nestled within the Scarlet Crusade's heavily...",sec={{t="Sanctum of Zealous Lore",b="Situated off the central nave of Tyr's Hand Abbey opposite the martial quarters, the Library Wing reflects the ideological core of the Scarlet Crusade. Within these quiet stone alcoves, priests and crusaders immerse themselves in theological tracts, militant doctrines, and writings twisted by years of relentless warfare against the Scourge. Rather than preserving open scholarship, the texts sheltered here fuel the Crusade's paranoia, reinforcing their conviction that all outsiders carry the taint of corruption.",sp=0},{t="Vessels of the Light",b="Beyond its collection of partisan scrolls and scriptures, the Library Wing serves as a repository for sacred items maintained by the Scarlet priesthood. In the back rooms of the wing, crusaders keep ritually consecrated supplies, including basins of pure holy water used in high-ranking liturgical rites. Reaching these inner sanctums requires fighting through elite Scarlet defenders who treat the library as both a bastion of faith and an impenetrable fortress.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Library Wing located?",a="The Library Wing is situated inside Tyr's Hand Abbey, found within the Scarlet Crusade enclave of Tyr's Hand in the southeastern Eastern Plaguelands. Inside the abbey, it lies south of the main entrance hall, opposite the Hall of Arms.",al={"library wing location","where is the library wing","how to find library wing tyr's hand"}},{q="What kinds of books are kept here?",a="The shelves hold theological texts of the Holy Light alongside militant doctrines and zealously curated literature produced by the Scarlet Crusade to justify their endless crusade against the undead and outsiders.",al={"what books are in the library","tyr's hand library tomes","what is stored in the library wing"}},{q="Who controls this part of the abbey?",a="The Library Wing is firmly held by the elite forces of the Scarlet Crusade, including clerics, scholars, and heavily armed defenders stationed to guard their doctrinal texts and sanctified supplies.",al={"who is in the library wing","who controls the library wing"}},{q="Is the Library Wing dangerous to visit?",a="Yes, it is exceptionally hazardous. The library is deep within Tyr's Hand, an elite Scarlet Crusade stronghold populated by high-level zealots who attack trespassers on sight.",al={"is the library wing safe","tyr's hand library difficulty"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="For holy practitioners, the Library Wing is a bitter display of how divine contemplation can be corrupted into narrow-minded extremism and paranoia.",["class:Paladin"]="Paladins view the wing as a perversion of the Silver Hand's original scholarly traditions, where devotion to the Light has been replaced by militant zealotry."},kw={"abbey","eastern plaguelands","holy water","library wing","propaganda","scarlet crusade","tomes","tyr's hand"},rel={"subzone:tyr-s-hand-abbey","subzone:tyr-s-hand","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:light"},src={"Library Wing (Tyr's Hand)"}}
E["subzone:light-s-hope-chapel"] = {t="subzone",n="Light's Hope Chapel",z="easternplaguelands",s="Light's Hope Chapel is a sacred sanctuary situated in the eastern reaches of the Plaguelands, serving as the primary redoubt and headquarters for the Argent Dawn. Once a secluded shrine of the Church of the Holy Light in the Eastweald, it now stands as an enduring bulwark against the Scourge. Beneath its consecrated soil lie the remains of a thousand fallen heroes of Lordaeron, protected from the Lich King's necromancy.",h="Light's Hope Chapel is a sacred sanctuary situated in the eastern reaches of the Plaguelands, serving as the...",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Plaguelands",b="Originally founded centuries ago as an outpost of the Church of the Holy Light within the verdant Eastweald, Light's Hope Chapel endured the fall of Lordaeron to become a vital shelter in a blighted realm. When the zealous extremists among the survivors splintered to form the Scarlet Crusade, more temperate knights and priests banded together to establish the Argent Dawn. Choosing this secluded, hallowed site as their forward base of operations, the Dawn opened its doors to all races and factions—Alliance and Horde alike—united in the common crusade to purge the Scourge and reclaim the northern lands.",sp=0},{t="The Consecrated Crypts",b="The strategic importance of Light's Hope Chapel goes far deeper than its surface fortifications. Following the Third War, Lord Maxwell Tyrosus and his comrades carried out a clandestine, solemn mission across Lordaeron, unearthing the bodies of a thousand revered heroes of the Light and reinterring them within the catacombs beneath the chapel. This mass reburial was enacted specifically to safeguard their sacred remains and righteous souls from being corrupted and raised into the Lich King's armies. As a result, the ground here radiates a profound holy power that the Scourge has repeatedly sought—and failed—to extinguish.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are Alliance and Horde working together at Light's Hope Chapel?",a="The Argent Dawn views the Scourge as an existential threat to all living beings, transcending the bitter politics of the Alliance and Horde. Unlike the fanatical and human-supremacist Scarlet Crusade, the Dawn actively recruits capable warriors, shamans, druids, and priests from any people willing to fight against the undead.",al={"why is horde allowed here","argent dawn neutral","cross faction base"}},{q="Who leads the defenders here?",a="Lord Maxwell Tyrosus leads the Argent Dawn from Light's Hope Chapel, having stepped up after the death of the order's first leader, Lord Raymond George. Tyrosus personally led the efforts to inter Lordaeron's fallen heroes in the chapel's catacombs and successfully repelled significant Scourge incursions against the outpost.",al={"who is in charge of lights hope","argent dawn leader","lord tyrosus"}},{q="Why is this chapel so sacred?",a="Beyond being an ancient holy site built during the early expansion of the Church of the Holy Light, the catacombs beneath the building hold the recovered remains of a thousand fallen champions of Lordaeron. The concentrated holy essence interred in the sacred ground shields these souls from being raised into undeath by the Lich King.",al={"what is under the chapel","why does the scourge want lights hope","sanctum beneath chapel"}},{q="What relationship does the chapel have with the Scarlet Crusade?",a="While the Argent Dawn formed from paladins and priests who rejected the unhinged zealotry and isolationism of the Scarlet Crusade, the Dawn still maintains cautious communication and negotiation with them at the chapel, viewing the Scourge as the preeminent enemy.",al={"are they friends with scarlet crusade","scarlet crusade lights hope","argent dawn vs scarlet crusade"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For holy warriors, Light's Hope Chapel is a sacred beacon in a sea of death, housing the consecrated tombs of the Silver Hand's greatest fallen champions.",["faction:Horde"]="Though situated deep in human territory and run by former Silver Hand knights, the chapel welcomes Horde fighters who prove their dedication to eradicating the undead."},kw={"argent dawn","consecrated ground","eastweald","holy light","lights hope","plaguelands","sanctum of light","tyrosus"},rel={"topic:argent-dawn","zone:easternplaguelands","npc:lord-maxwell-tyrosus","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:scourge","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:stratholme","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand"},src={"Light's Hope Chapel"}}
E["subzone:marris-stead"] = {t="subzone",n="Marris Stead",z="easternplaguelands",s="Perched on a ridge in the southwestern Eastern Plaguelands, the Marris Stead was once the peaceful family home of Lordaeron ranger Nathanos Marris. Following the devastation of the Third War, it now serves as the lonely, heavily defended redoubt of Nathanos Blightcaller, Champion of the Forsaken.",h="Perched on a ridge in the southwestern Eastern Plaguelands, the Marris Stead was once the peaceful family...",sec={{t="A Ranger's Ruined Home",b="Before the Third War, this homestead belonged to Nathanos Marris, a renowned human marksman and the only human ranger lord admitted into the Farstriders. When the Scourge tore through Lordaeron after the fall of Stratholme, the monstrous abomination Ramstein the Gorger cornered and slaughtered Nathanos at his own home. Raised as a mindless thrall bound to the Lich King, he was later discovered and liberated by Sylvanas Windrunner's rangers, breaking free of the Scourge to take his place among the Forsaken.",sp=0},{t="The Champion's Bastion",b="Now styling himself Nathanos Blightcaller, the champion returned to his ancestral farmstead alongside his pack of vicious blighthounds. Acting under orders from the Banshee Queen, he coordinates strikes across the Plaguelands against both the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade. The farmstead has also drawn the grim scrutiny of Stormwind's intelligence service: SI:7 operatives sent to investigate Forsaken activity here were slaughtered, leading the Alliance to uncover Nathanos's terrible transformation and place a heavy bounty upon his head.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who lives at Marris Stead?",a="The homestead is occupied by Nathanos Blightcaller, formerly known in life as the ranger Nathanos Marris. He resides here accompanied by his pack of blighthounds, serving as a frontline commander and Champion of the Banshee Queen.",al={"who is at marris stead","who lives here","npc at farm","nathanos location"}},{q="How did Nathanos become undead?",a="During the Third War, the Scourge overran Lordaeron. Despite his martial prowess, Nathanos was cornered at his farm and murdered by the abomination Ramstein the Gorger. He was raised into the Scourge until Lady Sylvanas Windrunner freed him into the Forsaken.",al={"how did nathanos die","nathanos death","who killed nathanos"}},{q="Why is the Alliance interested in this farm?",a="SI:7 spymaster Mathias Shaw dispatched an intelligence team to probe strange Forsaken movements in the area. When nearly all the scouts vanished, Alliance investigators discovered that the beloved ranger Nathanos had been raised as the Blightcaller, prompting Highlord Bolvar Fordragon to order a lethal strike against him.",al={"alliance marris stead","si7 plaguelands","why kill nathanos"},sp=1},{q="What artifacts are kept inside the house?",a="Several historic relics from the tragic Battle of Darrowshire are stored within the ruined farmhouse, including Davil Crokford's Libram and Redpath's Shield, collected amid the ongoing struggles in the Plaguelands.",al={"marris stead items","relics in house","darrowshire relics"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The discovery of what Nathanos has become is a bitter blow to the Alliance, turning this quiet homestead into the target of a high-priority military decapitation strike.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Forsaken and their Horde allies, the stead serves as an invaluable, heavily defended base of operations for waging war against the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade."},kw={"blighthounds","darrowshire relics","eastern plaguelands","marris stead","nathanos","nathanos blightcaller","nathanos marris","ramstein the gorger","si:7"},rel={"npc:nathanos-blightcaller","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:crown-guard-tower","subzone:darrowshire","quest:2300","npc:mathias-shaw"},src={"Marris Stead"}}
E["subzone:northdale"] = {t="subzone",n="Northdale",z="easternplaguelands",s="Northdale is a ruined settlement nestled north of Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands, near the border of Quel'Thalas. Once a thriving northern township, it now lies broken and overrun by banshees, shadowy watchers, and corrupted elementals. It is most famous as the bitter crossroads where Taelan Fordring abandoned the Order of the Silver Hand to embrace the fanaticism of the Scarlet Crusade.",h="Northdale is a ruined settlement nestled north of Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands, near the...",sec={{t="A Town of Sorrow",b="Situated along the hills north of Light's Hope Chapel, Northdale was once a peaceful community along the northern highway leading toward Quel'Thalas. The Third War left it in shattered ruins, its hearths cold and its population slain or driven out. Today, wailing banshees drift through the crumbling masonry, while invisible Eyeless Watchers lurk in the dark to survey the cursed roads. Even the nearby lake has succumbed to the plague, its waters bubbling with twisted, corrupted water elementals.",sp=0},{t="The Forsaken Oath",b="Northdale holds a dark significance in the tragic history of the Fordring family. Following the fall of Lordaeron and the dissolution of the Knights of the Silver Hand, young Taelan Fordring stood within these broken streets and formally cast aside his father's teachings. Believing the remnants of the Silver Hand too weak to purge the undead scourge, he surrendered his sacred duty and joined the radical ranks of the Scarlet Crusade, a fateful decision that shaped the crusade's hold over Hearthglen.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to Northdale?",a="Northdale was destroyed during the Third War when the Scourge swept through Lordaeron. Its buildings were razed and its people fell to the plague, leaving behind a husk of stone now haunted by vengeful spirits and corrupted elementals.",al={"why is northdale ruined","northdale history","what is northdale"}},{q="What significant event took place here?",a="It is the place where Taelan Fordring renounced the Order of the Silver Hand. Despairing over the fall of Lordaeron, he cast aside his paladin vows here and pledged himself to the emerging Scarlet Crusade.",al={"taelan fordring northdale","what happened to taelan","order of the silver hand northdale"}},{q="What creatures haunt the ruins today?",a="The town ruins are infested with wailing banshees and unseen Eyeless Watchers serving the Scourge. The adjacent waters are also spoiled, crawling with corrupted water elementals.",al={"mobs in northdale","northdale enemies","whats in northdale"}},{q="Where is Northdale located?",a="Northdale sits in the northeastern reaches of the Eastern Plaguelands, just north of Light's Hope Chapel and southeast of the Thalassian Pass into Quel'Thalas.",al={"northdale location","where is northdale","finding northdale"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For knights of the Light, Northdale is a sobering monument to lost faith—the very soil where Taelan Fordring abandoned the Silver Hand to chase vengeance.",["race:Human"]="The burnt foundations and wandering banshees of Northdale represent yet another lost Lordaeron community slaughtered and claimed by the Scourge."},kw={"banshee","eyeless watcher","fordring","northdale","plaguelands","scarlet crusade","silver hand","taelan"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:light"},src={"Northdale"}}
E["subzone:northpass-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Northpass Tower",z="easternplaguelands",s="Northpass Tower is a ruined Lordaeron scout tower situated in the northern reaches of the Eastern Plaguelands along the road to Quel'Thalas. Shattered during the Third War, its vantage point makes it a critical strategic prize in the escalating conflict between the Alliance and the Horde.",h="Northpass Tower is a ruined Lordaeron scout tower situated in the northern reaches of the Eastern Plaguelands...",sec={{t="Northern Sentinel",b="Built by the Kingdom of Lordaeron to guard the vital thoroughfare leading north into Quel'Thalas, Northpass Tower was reduced to a broken shell during the Scourge invasion. Despite its shattered stonework, the tower's elevated position retains immense tactical value, overlooking the blight-choked frontier between Stratholme's blighted outskirts and the distant elven lands.",sp=0},{t="Frontline Contention",b="With the Argent Dawn entrenched at Light's Hope Chapel, both the Alliance and the Horde seek to establish defensible outposts across the Plaguelands. Northpass Tower has become a frequent flashpoint, as securing its remnants bolsters regional supply lines and provides a forward foothold against both opposing factions and encroaching Scourge patrols.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Northpass Tower originally built for?",a="It was originally erected as an observation post by the Kingdom of Lordaeron to monitor the northern road leading toward the elven kingdom of Quel'Thalas.",al={"what is northpass tower","northpass history","why was northpass tower built"}},{q="Why is Northpass Tower in ruins?",a="It was destroyed alongside the rest of Lordaeron's northern defenses during the Scourge invasion in the Third War, leaving behind only cracked masonry and scaffolding.",al={"who destroyed northpass tower","why is northpass tower broken"}},{q="Why do the Alliance and Horde fight over this tower?",a="Both factions are pushing into the Plaguelands to counter the Scourge and each other. Holding Northpass Tower provides a fortified scout outpost and vital regional influence along the northern roads.",al={"why fight over northpass","who controls northpass tower"}},{q="Where does the road past Northpass Tower lead?",a="The road heads north directly toward the Thalassian border and the southern territory of Quel'Thalas.",al={"road past northpass tower","where does northern road go"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Reclaiming Northpass Tower represents a vital step toward restoring Lordaeron's fallen bastions and denying the Horde a staging ground in the north.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing this strategic ruin protects northern movements and fortifies the Horde's offensive against the Scourge and Alliance interlopers alike."},kw={"eastern plaguelands","lordaeron","northpass tower","quel'thalas","scourge","scout tower"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:crown-guard-tower","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","subzone:thondroril-river","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Northpass Tower"}}
E["subzone:noxious-glade"] = {t="subzone",n="Noxious Glade",z="easternplaguelands",s="Tucked away in the hills just north of Light's Hope Chapel, the Noxious Glade is a secluded basin steeped in concentrated plague. Choked with toxic green air and darkened soil, it functions as a nearby redoubt for Scourge operations right under the Argent Dawn's nose.",h="Tucked away in the hills just north of Light's Hope Chapel, the Noxious Glade is a secluded basin steeped in...",sec={{t="A Foul Foothold",b="While the Argent Dawn maintains its vigil at Light's Hope Chapel, an encampment of the Scourge lurks directly in the hills above them to the north. The Noxious Glade suffers from an infection far more severe than much of the surrounding terrain: the air hangs thick with a sickly green mist, and the soil has rotted into deep bruised purples. Within the hollow, the undead have erected ziggurats, a slaughterhouse for cobbling together abominations, and a plague cauldron that continuously spews pestilence into the atmosphere.",sp=0},{t="Under the Dawn's Gaze",b="Because of its close proximity to the chapel, the glade poses a persistent threat to travelers, couriers, and holy warriors working out of Light's Hope. The Scourge forces entrenched here construct foul monstrosities and brew toxins undisturbed by the sunlight, kept hidden by the surrounding natural ridge until an unwary traveler climbs the path directly into their midst.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Noxious Glade located?",a="The Noxious Glade lies tucked in the hills immediately north of Light's Hope Chapel in the eastern reaches of the Eastern Plaguelands.",al={"where is noxious glade","noxious glade location","how to get to noxious glade"}},{q="Why is the air and ground a different color here?",a="The glade is heavily blighted even compared to the rest of the Plaguelands. A functioning plague cauldron and nearby Scourge structures pump unceasing toxins into the hollow, dyeing the earth dark purple and shrouding the clearing in a poisonous green haze.",al={"why is it green","why is ground purple","noxious glade blight"}},{q="What Scourge structures are in the glade?",a="The clearing features classic Scourge architecture, including a towering plague cauldron, several ziggurats, and a slaughterhouse used to assemble monstrous constructs like abominations.",al={"what is inside noxious glade","noxious glade buildings"}},{q="Does the Argent Dawn know about this place?",a="Yes, but with their resources constantly stretched thin defending against massed Scourge onslaughts across the Plaguelands, outposts like the Noxious Glade remain dangerous festering pockets just over the chapel's perimeter.",al={"lights hope chapel aware","argent dawn noxious glade"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The glade serves as an alarming reminder of how close Scourge blight creeps to the holy sanctuary of Light's Hope Chapel, offering plenty of undead abominations and necromancers to purge.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken champions will recognize the slaughterhouses and plague cauldrons here as typical tools of the Lich King's grip, starkly demonstrating the fate awaiting those who do not break free."},kw={"blight","eastern plaguelands","light's hope chapel","noxious glade","plague cauldron","scourge","slaughterhouse","ziggurat"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","subzone:cauldron","topic:scourge","topic:light"},src={"Noxious Glade"}}
E["subzone:pestilent-scar"] = {t="subzone",n="Pestilent Scar",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Pestilent Scar is a deep, blighted gorge carved into the blighted terrain of the Eastern Plaguelands. Unlike the jagged rents torn open by catastrophic Scourge blight, this chasm appears to be a natural canyon or dried lakebed that was subsequently corrupted and overrun by ravenous oozes.",h="The Pestilent Scar is a deep, blighted gorge carved into the blighted terrain of the Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Blighted Chasm",b="Winding through the eastern reaches of the Eastern Plaguelands, the Pestilent Scar forms a gloomy rift in the corrupted landscape. While nearby rifts like the Infectis Scar were ripped into the earth by sudden catastrophic eruptions of the Plague of Undeath, scholars note that the Pestilent Scar seems to have originated as a natural geological formation. It was likely a deep river canyon or natural lake that dried up when the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, leaving a barren trench that gradually pooled with noxious runoff and foul slime.",sp=0},{t="The Slime Pits",b="Deprived of pure water and bathed in persistent unholy decay, the hollow has become a breeding pit for mutated, acidic slimes and carrion vermin. Traveling near its crumbling rim is treacherous; the air above the drop is choked with acrid fumes, and the unstable soil frequently threatens to dump unwary adventurers straight into the churning muck below.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Pestilent Scar?",a="The Pestilent Scar is a sunken gorge located in the Eastern Plaguelands. Corrupted during the fall of Lordaeron, the canyon is filled with foul runoff, diseased soil, and aggressive ooze monstrosities.",al={"pestilent scar lore","what is pestilent scar","pestilent scar canyon"}},{q="How did the Pestilent Scar form?",a="Unlike the unnatural fissures torn through the earth by catastrophic Scourge eruptions, the Pestilent Scar appears to have been a natural valley, lake, or river canyon that dried up and withered under the blight of the Plague of Undeath.",al={"how was pestilent scar made","pestilent scar origin","who made pestilent scar"}},{q="How does it differ from the Infectis Scar?",a="The Infectis Scar was violently ripped open as an unnatural volcanic rupture oozing pure magical blight. The Pestilent Scar is an older, natural land depression that gradually collected corruption and runoff after the land died.",al={"pestilent scar vs infectis scar","infectis scar difference"}},{q="What creatures live in the Pestilent Scar?",a="The chasm floor is dominated by acidic, plague-spawned oozes and carrion-eating vermin that thrive within the poisonous pools and rotting organic matter trapped at the bottom.",al={"pestilent scar mobs","what lives in pestilent scar"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="The edges of the gorge are steeped in concentrated rot, sometimes nurturing rare, blight-hardened flora like Arthas' Tears and Plaguebloom along its cliffs.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken apothecaries frequently study the slimes residing within such deep fissures to isolate unstable variations of the Scourge's foulest toxins."},kw={"blight","eastern plaguelands","gorge","infectis scar","oozes","pestilent scar","slime"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:infectis-scar","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:light"},src={"Pestilent Scar"}}
E["subzone:plaguewood"] = {t="subzone",n="Plaguewood",z="easternplaguelands",s="Once a peaceful woodland known as Greenwood, the Plaguewood is now a blighted, fungus-choked expanse stretching south of Stratholme. Crawling with Scourge infrastructure and patrolling Scarlet Crusaders, it stands as one of the most corrupt corners of the Eastern Plaguelands.",h="Once a peaceful woodland known as Greenwood, the Plaguewood is now a blighted, fungus-choked expanse...",sec={{t="From Greenwood to Decay",b="Before the Third War, this region was Greenwood, a vibrant forest that mirrored the lush woods of Elwynn. A modest village sat near its entrance, and its roads were traveled by farmers and soldiers alike. All of that collapsed when tainted grain arrived from Andorhal. Today, spongy, corrupted soil has taken the place of rich earth, and titanic mushrooms dwarf the dead trees, constantly spewing noxious brown vapors across the woodland floor.",sp=0},{t="A Bastion of the Dead",b="Now completely claimed by the Scourge, the Plaguewood serves as a grim staging ground for the undead surrounding Stratholme. Ziggurats and slaughterhouses dot the decayed landscape, churning out abominations and cultists. To make matters worse for travelers, fanatic Scarlet Crusaders relentlessly patrol the road toward Stratholme's gates, eager to purge the Scourge and brutally slaughter any living wanderers they encounter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was this forest called before the plague?",a="Prior to the Third War, the region was known as Greenwood. It was a thriving forest with a small village near its entrance, very similar in beauty and climate to Elwynn Forest.",al={"plaguewood old name","greenwood lore","what was plaguewood"}},{q="Why are there massive mushrooms growing everywhere?",a="The plague fundamentally warped the local ecology. The soil turned spongy, and monstrous fungi sprouted across the forest floor, belching noxious brown clouds that resemble the vapors of plague cauldrons.",al={"giant mushrooms plaguewood","fungus plaguewood","why mushrooms"}},{q="Who controls the Plaguewood today?",a="The forest is overwhelmingly held by the Scourge, complete with necromancers, ghouls, ziggurats, and slaughterhouses. In addition, patrols from the Scarlet Crusade regularly march along the main roads, attacking the undead and any living travelers on sight.",al={"who rules plaguewood","plaguewood enemies","who lives in plaguewood"}},{q="Where does the road through the woods lead?",a="The main road cuts directly north into the gates of the fallen city of Stratholme, while the western expanses of the blighted woods stretch out toward the ruined village of Terrordale.",al={"plaguewood road destination","where does path go","stratholme road"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The twisted trees and foul cauldrons of the Plaguewood serve as a harrowing reminder of Lordaeron's fall, testing any champion of the Light against swarms of abominations and unyielding fanatics.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance survivors, walking these paths means seeing the very road Prince Arthas took toward his infamous purge of Stratholme, now drowned in rot and mad Scarlet zealots."},kw={"fungus","greenwood","plaguewood","scourge","slaughterhouses","stratholme","terrordale","ziggurats"},rel={"subzone:stratholme","zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:terrordale","topic:scourge","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:lordaeron","subzone:andorhal","zone:elwynn"},src={"Plaguewood"}}
E["subzone:plaguewood-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Plaguewood Tower",z="easternplaguelands",s="Plaguewood Tower is a ruined Lordaeron scout tower situated in the northern reaches of the Plaguewood near Terrordale. Shattered during the Scourge invasion, its strategic vantage point makes it a critical contested redoubt for Alliance and Horde forces striving to establish footholds in the Eastern Plaguelands.",h="Plaguewood Tower is a ruined Lordaeron scout tower situated in the northern reaches of the Plaguewood near...",sec={{t="A Ruined Sentinel in the North",b="Standing on the edge of the blight-choked Plaguewood and the blighted town of Terrordale, Plaguewood Tower once served the Kingdom of Lordaeron as a vital northern watchpost. When the Scourge swept across the land, the fortification was battered into crumbling masonry and left in ruins amid corrupted fungal canopies. Today, despite its fractured state, the tower retains immense tactical importance. Because it commands the northern trails and monitors nearby undead movements, both the Alliance and the Horde regularly dispatch scouts to seize and hold its footprint, turning the stone remnants into an active battleground against both the Scourge and each other.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Plaguewood Tower originally used for?",a="Plaguewood Tower was built by the Kingdom of Lordaeron as a regional watchtower. Before the Third War, guards stationed here watched over the northern forests, roads, and settlements like Terrordale before the Scourge overwhelmed and shattered the garrison.",al={"original purpose","who built plaguewood tower","history of tower"}},{q="Why are the Alliance and Horde fighting over this ruin?",a="Even in ruins, the high ground and stonework provide a vital outpost. Both factions seek to establish forward positions deep in the Plaguelands to counter Scourge movements, secure supply lines, and bolster their overall foothold in the region.",al={"why capture tower","tower battlefield","pvp tower"}},{q="Where exactly is the tower located?",a="It is positioned in the northern sector of the Eastern Plaguelands within the Plaguewood, just outside the ruined town of Terrordale and north of Stratholme's outer blighted reaches.",al={"tower location","where is plaguewood tower","map location"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance forces, reclaiming the shattered watchtowers of Lordaeron is both a logistical necessity for surviving the Plaguelands and a symbolic reclamation of fallen human lands.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde relies on securing ruined fortifications like Plaguewood Tower to establish defensive outposts and challenge Alliance expansion throughout the northern kingdoms."},kw={"eastern plaguelands","lordaeron","outpost","plaguewood","plaguewood tower","scourge","terrordale","watchtower"},rel={"subzone:plaguewood","subzone:terrordale","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:horde","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel"},src={"Plaguewood Tower"}}
E["subzone:quel-lithien-lodge"] = {t="subzone",n="Quel'Lithien Lodge",z="easternplaguelands",s="Quel'Lithien Lodge is an isolated high elven refuge nestled in the forested northern hills of the Eastern Plaguelands near the border of Quel'Thalas. Led by Renthar Hawkspear, its Farstrider rangers are exiles from their homeland who reject the radical magical practices adopted by their kin in Silvermoon. Surrounded by the Scourge and hunted by Forsaken scouts, the lodge clings to survival while guarding centuries-old elven archives.",h="Quel'Lithien Lodge is an isolated high elven refuge nestled in the forested northern hills of the Eastern...",sec={{t="A Bitter Exile",b="Before the Third War, Quel'Lithien was a favored woodland retreat for the Farstriders of Quel'Thalas, frequently visited by veteran rangers like Lor'themar Theron. Its fortune soured when the elven kingdom was ravaged by the Scourge and new magical teachings were brought back to ease the survivors' withdrawal. Renthar Hawkspear and a cohort of rangers fiercely objected to these dubious methods on moral grounds. Unwilling to endure internal discord while struggling to rebuild, Regent Lord Lor'themar banished the dissenters south. Renthar led his followers to Quel'Lithien Lodge, where they maintain their high elven identity, severed from their home yet resolutely standing apart from the corrupted ruins surrounding them.",sp=0},{t="Hunted in the Plaguelands",b="The rangers' quiet vigil has not gone unnoticed. Deep within the tainted woods, Nathanos Blightcaller—once the solitary human Ranger Lord trained alongside these very elves—has directed Horde champions to infiltrate Quel'Lithien Lodge. Nathanos seeks the Quel'Thalas Registry, an official record containing details of the ranger order and elven lineages, ordering the slaughter of the lodge's defenders to retrieve it. Cut off from Silvermoon and refusing aid, the rangers at Quel'Lithien find themselves besieged by former allies and the surrounding undead alike.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are there living high elves in the Eastern Plaguelands?",a="The lodge's inhabitants are Farstriders and priests who were banished from Quel'Thalas by Regent Lord Lor'themar Theron. They refused to adopt the dark, desperate methods taught to cope with the destruction of the Sunwell, choosing exile over what they viewed as a moral corruption of their people.",al={"why high elves here","who lives at quel'lithien","quellithien elves"}},{q="Who leads Quel'Lithien Lodge?",a="The lodge is led by Renthar Hawkspear, a veteran elven ranger captain who commanded hunters here as far back as the Second War. Following his disagreement with Silvermoon's leadership, he guided the exiled dissenters to the lodge to make a stand together.",al={"quellithien leader","renthar hawkspear","who is renthar"}},{q="Are the elves at Quel'Lithien Lodge part of the Alliance?",a="No. While they are friendly to Alliance travelers and openly hostile toward the Horde, the lodge functions as an entirely autonomous high elven settlement receiving no formal support or direction from Stormwind or Ironforge.",al={"are quellithien elves alliance","quellithien faction"}},{q="Why does Nathanos Blightcaller target the lodge?",a="Nathanos Blightcaller sends Horde agents to attack the lodge specifically to secure the Quel'Thalas Registry, an important historical document chronicling elven ranger personnel and records that remains stored in the lodge's archives.",al={"why nathanos attack quellithien","the ranger lord's behest","quel'thalas registry"}},{q="How does Quel'Lithien differ from Quel'Danil Lodge?",a="Both were historic high elven hunting lodges, but Quel'Danil is situated safely among friendly Wildhammer dwarves in the Hinterlands. Quel'Lithien sits isolated on the frontline of the Eastern Plaguelands, trapped between the blighted ruins and the closed gates of Quel'Thalas.",al={"queldanil vs quellithien","hinterlands lodge comparison"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The Farstriders stationed here represent centuries of classical Thalassian marksmanship, maintaining their survival skills in a hostile wilderness completely cut off from civil society.",["faction:Horde"]="Operating on orders from Nathanos Blightcaller out of the Marris Stead, Horde champions are dispatched here on a deadly mission to seize high elven records through sheer force."},kw={"aurora skycaller","farstrider","high elves","marris stead","quel'lithien","quel'thalas registry","quellithien","renthar hawkspear"},rel={"npc:nathanos-blightcaller","npc:lor-themar-theron","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","topic:alliance","topic:horde","topic:third-war"},src={"Quel'Lithien Lodge"}}
E["subzone:sanctum-of-light"] = {t="subzone",n="Sanctum of Light",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Sanctum of Light is a secret underground catacomb beneath Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands. Created during the Third War, it holds the relocated remains of a thousand fallen champions of Lordaeron to protect them from Scourge necromancy.",h="The Sanctum of Light is a secret underground catacomb beneath Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Hidden Resting Place",b="During the fall of Lordaeron in the Third War, Lord Maxwell Tyrosus and a devoted few undertook a covert mission to prevent the Scourge from raising the realm's greatest defenders into unholy servitude. Exhuming the bodies of a thousand noble paladins, priests, and warriors across Lordaeron—including renowned heroes such as Killoren—they brought them deep into the eastern frontier and reinterred them in hallowed catacombs beneath Light's Hope Chapel. Shielded by potent blessings of the Light, this hidden crypt protects the righteous dead from the defiling grasp of the Lich King.",sp=0},{t="The Foundation of Light's Hope",b="The presence of these honored remains explains why the Argent Dawn chose Light's Hope Chapel as their primary stronghold in the Eastern Plaguelands. After splitting away from the zealots who would form the Scarlet Crusade, Tyrosus and his comrades established their vanguard directly above the Sanctum to ensure the catacombs would never fall into enemy hands. The concentrated sanctity of a thousand uncorrupted heroes permeates the earth, transforming the chapel above into an enduring bastion of holy power amid a sea of undeath.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sanctum of Light?",a="It is a consecrated catacomb buried directly beneath Light's Hope Chapel. It houses the remains of a thousand heroes of Lordaeron, placed there to safeguard their corpses and souls from being raised by the Scourge.",al={"what is sanctum of light","underneath lights hope","lights hope catacombs"}},{q="Who created the Sanctum?",a="Lord Maxwell Tyrosus and a select group of righteous allies exhumed the bodies from churchyards across fallen Lordaeron during the Third War and laid them to rest here in secret.",al={"who built the sanctum of light","who put bodies under lights hope","maxwell tyrosus catacombs"}},{q="Why are the bodies buried here instead of their original graves?",a="The Lich King's necromancers actively sought the remains of mighty champions to bolster the Scourge's ranks. Tyrosus gathered and reinterred them under powerful holy protections so their martial and spiritual might could never be used against the living.",al={"why exhumed","why moved to lights hope","scourge raising heroes"}},{q="Can players enter the Sanctum of Light?",a="No. The catacombs beneath the chapel are sealed and guarded in secret by the Argent Dawn, hidden from view to ensure the sacred dead remain undisturbed.",al={"how to get in","can i go inside","sanctum entrance"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The catacombs enshrine the uncorrupted remains of the Order of the Silver Hand's early heroes, preserved by Lord Maxwell Tyrosus to protect their legacy from the Scourge.",["class:Priest"]="The concentrated faith and sanctity of a thousand holy souls buried beneath the chapel give Light's Hope its remarkable aura of purity amidst the surrounding plague."},kw={"argent dawn","catacombs","eastern plaguelands","killoren","light's hope chapel","lord maxwell tyrosus","lordaeron","sanctum of light"},rel={"subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","zone:easternplaguelands","npc:lord-maxwell-tyrosus","topic:argent-dawn","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","topic:third-war"},src={"Sanctum of Light"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-base-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Base Camp",z="easternplaguelands",s="Scarlet Base Camp is a fortified outpost established on the eastern shore of Lake Mereldar in the Eastern Plaguelands. Guarded by zealous paladins, inquisitors, and foot soldiers, it protects the approaches leading toward Tyr's Hand. The camp serves as a forward defensive line shielding local Scarlet personnel and refugees from the unrelenting Scourge.",h="Scarlet Base Camp is a fortified outpost established on the eastern shore of Lake Mereldar in the Eastern...",sec={{t="A Forward Line on Lake Mereldar",b="Perched on the eastern banks of Lake Mereldar, the Scarlet Base Camp functions as an entrenched defensive perimeter just west of Tyr's Hand. Fortified with timber barricades, tents, and sentry watch posts, it provides early warning against undead incursions roaming the Plaguelands. Under the command of leaders like Commander Beatrix alongside Scarlet inquisitors and sergeants, the encampment maintains discipline among troops and provides a heavily defended rallying point for refugees fleeing the surrounding blighted wilderness.",sp=0},{t="Shielding the Bastion",b="Because Tyr's Hand is one of the Crusade's supreme strongholds in Lordaeron, securing its approaches across the lake is vital. The soldiers stationed here harbor deep fanaticism, viewing any outsider who approaches as a potential carrier of the plague or an outright agent of darkness. Together with armed infantry and inquisitors, the camp maintains an aggressive vigil over the eastern waters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Scarlet Base Camp?",a="The Scarlet Base Camp serves as an outer defensive perimeter and forward watch on the eastern bank of Lake Mereldar. It monitors the roadways and waters leading directly to the Scarlet Crusade's fortified bastion of Tyr's Hand, warding off wandering Scourge and sheltering affiliated refugees.",al={"what is scarlet base camp","why is scarlet camp here","purpose of base camp"}},{q="Who leads the forces stationed at the camp?",a="The encampment is led by Commander Beatrix, supported by inquisitors such as Inquisitor Jociphine and Scarlet Inquisitor Caldoran, who ensure both martial readiness and zealous ideological purity among the infantry and sergeants.",al={"who leads scarlet base camp","camp commander","scarlet camp leaders"}},{q="Are the occupants hostile to travelers?",a="Yes. Like nearly all elements of the Scarlet Crusade in the Plaguelands, the troops and inquisitors at this camp view all outsiders—Horde and Alliance alike—as contaminated, untrustworthy, or disguised agents of the Scourge, attacking anyone who draws near.",al={"will scarlet base camp attack me","is scarlet camp hostile","are they friendly"}},{q="Why are there refugees at this outpost?",a="The refugees present at the camp are humans fleeing the devastation of the Eastern Plaguelands who look to the military might of Tyr's Hand for protection. They congregate around the barricaded outpost where Scarlet infantry offer a protective perimeter against the undead.",al={"why are there refugees here","tyrs hand refugees","who are the refugees"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The camp reflects the tragic corruption of the Silver Hand's legacy, where righteous zeal in the defense of Lordaeron's holy ground has warped into aggressive paranoia against fellow survivors.",["race:Undead"]="The outpost serves as a direct reminder of the living zealots who wish to purge the Forsaken from Lordaeron just as ruthlessly as they hunt the mindless Scourge."},kw={"caldoran","commander beatrix","eastern plaguelands","inquisitor jociphine","lake mereldar","scarlet base camp","scarlet crusade","tyr's hand"},rel={"subzone:lake-mereldar","subzone:tyr-s-hand","zone:easternplaguelands"},src={"Scarlet Base Camp"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-basilica"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Basilica",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Scarlet Basilica is a grand cathedral standing at the heart of Tyr's Hand in the Eastern Plaguelands. It serves as the high seat of spiritual and military authority for the Scarlet Crusade in the east. Overseen by Crusader Lord Valdelmar, its halls represent the zealots' unyielding bastion against the Scourge.",h="The Scarlet Basilica is a grand cathedral standing at the heart of Tyr's Hand in the Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="Heart of the Eastern Crusade",b="Rising prominently over the fortified enclave of Tyr's Hand, the Scarlet Basilica acts as the central cathedral and command hub for the Scarlet Crusade's operations in the Eastern Plaguelands. While the Scarlet Monastery far to the west in Tirisfal Glades serves as the order's spiritual heart, this basilica anchors their surviving territorial stronghold against the blighted horrors of Lordaeron. Guarded fiercely by elite crusaders, the cathedral houses Crusader Lord Valdelmar, who directs the local defense and zealously purges any outsiders who dare approach.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Scarlet Basilica?",a="The Scarlet Basilica is the grand cathedral located inside the fortress city of Tyr's Hand in the Eastern Plaguelands. It serves as the primary seat of religious and military authority for the Scarlet Crusade in the region.",al={"scarlet basilica info","what is this cathedral","tyrs hand church"}},{q="Who leads the forces inside the Basilica?",a="Crusader Lord Valdelmar commands the forces within the Scarlet Basilica, standing as one of the Scarlet Crusade's high-ranking leaders holding Tyr's Hand against the Scourge and other perceived enemies.",al={"who is in scarlet basilica","valdelmar","scarlet basilica boss"}},{q="How does this compare to the Scarlet Monastery?",a="While the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades is the order's primary spiritual headquarters, the Scarlet Basilica functions as their eastern counterpart, providing a commanding religious and fortified center deep within the Plaguelands.",al={"monastery vs basilica","is this the scarlet monastery"}},{q="Are travelers welcome inside the Basilica?",a="No. The Scarlet Crusade has descended into xenophobic madness, believing that anyone not clad in their crimson colors is tainted by undeath. Both Alliance and Horde intruders are attacked immediately on sight.",al={"can alliance enter","is scarlet basilica hostile","can i visit"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The basilica stands as a twisted monument to holy devotion gone astray, where former knights of the Silver Hand have turned their fervor into merciless fanaticism.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the basilica represents one of the most entrenched outposts of the zealots who actively seek the total eradication of all undead regardless of free will."},kw={"cathedral","crusader lord valdelmar","eastern plaguelands","scarlet basilica","scarlet crusade","tyr's hand"},rel={"subzone:tyr-s-hand","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:tyr-s-hand-abbey","subzone:high-seat","zone:scarlet","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Scarlet Basilica"}}
E["subzone:stratholme"] = {t="subzone",n="Stratholme",z="easternplaguelands",s="Stratholme was once the jewel of the Eastweald and the second greatest city in the Kingdom of Lordaeron. During the Third War, it became the site of Prince Arthas Menethil's infamous culling after its citizens consumed grain tainted by the Plague of Undeath. Today, the ruined metropolis still burns, serving as the Scourge's primary stronghold in northern Lordaeron.",h="Stratholme was once the jewel of the Eastweald and the second greatest city in the Kingdom of Lordaeron.",sec={{t="Cradle of Paladins and Trade",b="Long before its downfall, Stratholme stood as a cornerstone of northern civilization. Emerging centuries ago from the Arathi expansion into the Eastweald, it flourished into Lordaeron's second-largest settlement, renowned for holy shrines and sacred water capable of resisting dark sorcery. Prior to the Second War, Archbishop Alonsus Faol gathered at the city's chapel to establish the Order of the Knights of the Silver Hand, ordaining legends like Uther the Lightbringer. Throughout that war, Stratholme served as a vital port, supply hub, and northern oil refinery for the Alliance of Lordaeron, enduring an assault by the Old Horde before rebuilding in victory.",sp=0},{t="The Culling and Eternal Ruin",b="Stratholme's fate was sealed when the Cult of the Damned funneled shipments of infected grain from Andorhal into the city's markets. Unaware, thousands ate the tainted flour. When Prince Arthas arrived alongside Uther and Jaina Proudmoore, he discovered the infection had spread too far to cure. Deeming slaughter the only way to deny Mal'Ganis an entire army, Arthas ordered the purge of every citizen—an atrocity that drove Uther and Jaina away and began the prince's descent into madness. The city was put to the torch, and in the aftermath, the Scourge moved into the smoking ruins to make it their regional capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Stratholme still burning?",a="When Prince Arthas purged the city during the Third War, his forces set fire to homes and streets to eradicate the infected populace and halt the spread of undeath. The unnatural, plague-tainted blaze has lingered ever since, fed by dark necromantic energies and the rampant Scourge infestation.",al={"why is stratholme on fire","fire in stratholme","stratholme smoke"}},{q="What was the Culling of Stratholme?",a="The Culling was the wholesale slaughter of Stratholme's populace by Prince Arthas Menethil. After the city consumed grain infected with the Plague of Undeath, Arthas chose to execute every inhabitant—sick or healthy—before they could rise as soldiers for the Scourge, a decision that fractured his alliances and broke his moral compass.",al={"the culling","arthas purge","purge of stratholme"}},{q="What historic role did Stratholme play for the Silver Hand?",a="Stratholme is the birthplace of the Knights of the Silver Hand. In the city's Alonsus Chapel, Archbishop Alonsus Faol founded the paladin order before the Second War and anointed its first five members, including Uther the Lightbringer, Turalyon, and Saidan Dathrohan.",al={"silver hand origin","alonsus chapel","order of the silver hand stratholme"}},{q="What happened to Tirion Fordring here?",a="Years after the Second War, Highlord Tirion Fordring was tried for treason in Stratholme's Hall of Justice for defending the honorable orc hermit Eitrigg. Judged by Uther and Alliance leaders, Tirion was stripped of his title and exiled. He later freed Eitrigg amidst an attack on the city led by Thrall.",al={"tirion fordring trial","tirion trial stratholme","eitrigg trial"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For paladins, Stratholme is hallowed ground transformed into tragedy; it is the site where the Order of the Silver Hand was born, and where Arthas shattered that same brotherhood by demanding the slaughter of innocent citizens.",["faction:Alliance"]="The ruined city stands as a haunting monument to Lordaeron's fall, reminding Alliance travelers of the devastating price paid when the northern kingdoms collapsed to plague and treachery."},kw={"andorhal","arthas","culling","eastweald","mal'ganis","plaguelands","scourge","silver hand","stratholme","uther"},rel={"topic:arthas-menethil","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","topic:scourge","topic:plague-of-undeath","subzone:andorhal","npc:tirion-fordring","topic:lordaeron","zone:easternplaguelands"},src={"Stratholme"}}
E["subzone:stratholme-classic"] = {t="subzone",n="Stratholme (Classic)",z="easternplaguelands",s="Stratholme, once northern Lordaeron's proudest jewel and the birthplace of the Silver Hand, is now a burning ruin serving as the Scourge's regional capital. Divided between the fanatical Scarlet Crusade and Baron Rivendare's undead legions, the cursed city remains locked in endless, violent war.",h="Stratholme, once northern Lordaeron's proudest jewel and the birthplace of the Silver Hand, is now a burning...",sec={{t="The Cursed Capital",b="Before the Third War, Stratholme was the northern powerhouse of Lordaeron and the sacred birthplace of the Knights of the Silver Hand. Its fate was sealed when Prince Arthas purged the city, slaughtering his own subjects after infected grain brought the plague within its walls. Left smoldering and ruined, Stratholme was claimed by the Scourge. Today, under the overarching authority of the lich Kel'Thuzad and the field command of Baron Rivendare, the city serves as the primary base for undead power in the Plaguelands.",sp=0},{t="A Divided Warfront",b="Stratholme is split between two vicious factions locked in perpetual bloodshed. To the west, the fanatical Scarlet Crusade has fortified Crusaders' Square and the Scarlet Bastion, commanded by Grand Crusader Saidan Dathrohan. To the east lies the Scourge slaughterhouses and necropolises, defended by towering ziggurats and the death knight Baron Rivendare. Anyone entering the city must navigate this grinding crossfire, surrounded by burning tenements and restless spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Stratholme still burning?",a="Prince Arthas set fire to the city during his infamous purge in the Third War to stop the plague of undeath from spreading. The fires have never truly gone out, kept smoldering by dark magic, necromancy, and the endless urban warfare between the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"why is stratholme on fire","who burned stratholme","stratholme burning"}},{q="Who controls Stratholme right now?",a="Control is divided. Grand Crusader Dathrohan commands a surviving contingent of the Scarlet Crusade fortified in the western bastion, while the death knight Baron Rivendare governs the eastern ruins for the Scourge under Kel'Thuzad.",al={"who rules stratholme","who is in charge of stratholme","stratholme leaders"}},{q="What is the historical significance of the city to paladins?",a="Stratholme was the birthplace of the Order of the Silver Hand, where Archbishop Alonsus Faol first consecrated Uther the Lightbringer and the original paladins. Its downfall marks the deepest tragedy in the order's history.",al={"silver hand stratholme","paladin history stratholme"}},{q="How do you enter the Scourge-controlled side of the city?",a="While adventurers can fight all the way through from the main gate, the eastern Scourge district can also be reached directly via the Service Entrance. Entering through this back gate requires a key held by Magistrate Barthilas, though skilled rogues, powerful blacksmith skeleton keys, or goblin explosives can also breach it.",al={"back door key","service entrance stratholme","how to get into undead side"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The desecration of Stratholme cuts deeply for paladins; it is both the sacred birthplace of the Silver Hand and the graveyard where Arthas shattered Uther's guidance.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Stratholme represents the catastrophic fall of Lordaeron, reminding soldiers and survivors of the terrible cost of the Third War."},kw={"arthas","dathrohan","plaguelands","purge","rivendare","silver hand","slaughterhouse","stratholme"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:lordaeron","topic:third-war","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lich-king","topic:light"},src={"Stratholme (Classic)"}}
E["subzone:stratholme-main-gate"] = {t="subzone",n="Stratholme Main Gate",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Stratholme Main Gate stands as the grand, burning entrance to Lordaeron's northern metropolis in the northwestern Eastern Plaguelands. It provides direct access through the city's ruined avenues toward King's Square and the crusader fortifications within.",h="The Stratholme Main Gate stands as the grand, burning entrance to Lordaeron's northern metropolis in the...",sec={{t="Gateway to a Fallen Jewel",b="Stratholme was once the pride of northern Lordaeron, famed as the birthplace of the Order of the Silver Hand. Today, its colossal arched main gates mark the threshold of an ongoing nightmare. It was here during the Third War that Prince Arthas turned on his mentor, Uther the Lightbringer, and purged his own citizens before the Plague of Undeath could claim them. The city has burned relentlessly ever since, transformed into the primary Scourge stronghold in the region.",sp=0},{t="The Scarlet Approach",b="Approaching through the main gate leads straight into the ruins of King's Square and Market Row, heading toward the fortified district known as the Scarlet Bastion. Zealots of the Scarlet Crusade pushed through this entrance to reclaim the city and purge the dead, carving out an encampment in the ruins. However, the crusaders find themselves surrounded by overwhelming undead monstrosities, fighting an attrition war they cannot win against the dark forces orchestrating Stratholme's defense.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this gate lead?",a="The main gate is the grand front portal into Stratholme, opening directly into King's Square and Market Row. It serves as the primary route toward the Scarlet Bastion, the district contested by the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"where does strat main gate go","what is stratholme main gate","front entrance strat"}},{q="Why is the city behind these gates still burning?",a="During the Third War, Prince Arthas purged the city and set it ablaze to stop the spread of the Plague of Undeath. Dark necromantic magic, unholy fires, and rampant Scourge corruption have kept the ruined city smoldering and burning without pause ever since.",al={"why is stratholme on fire","who burned stratholme","fire in stratholme"}},{q="What is the difference between this gate and the Service Entrance?",a="Both entryways lead into the same vast ruined city, but from opposite ends. The Main Gate enters near the living and scarlet-held quarters of the city, whereas the Service Entrance opens into the eastern streets directly under the thrall of the Scourge slaughterhouses and Baron Rivendare.",al={"main gate vs service entrance","which strat entrance","strat doors"}},{q="Who controls the area immediately inside the Main Gate?",a="The initial streets beyond the archway are prowled by shambling zombies, ghouls, skeletal horrors, and wandering shades, while the Scarlet Crusade maintains an embattled bastion further into the avenues.",al={"who is inside main gate","what mobs are at strat front"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Standing before these gates carries immense grief for paladins; this is where the Silver Hand fractured when Arthas disbanded the order on the day he purged Stratholme.",["race:Human"]="The main archway was once the grand threshold of Lordaeron's second-greatest capital, now reduced to an ash-choked necropolis."},kw={"arthas","eastern plaguelands","front entrance","king's square","main gate","scarlet bastion","scourge","stratholme"},rel={"subzone:stratholme","subzone:stratholme-service-entrance","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","topic:third-war","topic:plague-of-undeath"},src={"Stratholme Main Gate"}}
E["subzone:stratholme-service-entrance"] = {t="subzone",n="Stratholme Service Entrance",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Stratholme Service Entrance is a fortified rear gateway located at Eastwall Gate in the northern Eastern Plaguelands. It provides direct, covert access into the Scourge-controlled eastern quarter of the burning city, bypassing the grand front gates.",h="The Stratholme Service Entrance is a fortified rear gateway located at Eastwall Gate in the northern Eastern...",sec={{t="A Breached Bastion",b="While the monumental Main Gate of Stratholme opens into King's Square and the crusader-held districts, the Service Entrance breaches the city's eastern fortification at Eastwall Gate. In Lordaeron's prime, this passage allowed supply convoys and municipal workers into the city's utility corridors without disrupting traffic along the main boulevards. Today, it leads directly into the corrupted heart of the metropolis: Elders' Square and the blighted pathways leading toward Baron Rivendare's slaughterhouses.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge Redoubt",b="Venturing through the service portal avoids the Scarlet Crusade garrisons near the front entrance, plunging straight into Scourge territory. The surrounding alleys crawl with gargoyles, crypt fiends, and cultists guarding the dread ziggurats. For the Argent Dawn and daring adventurers seeking to strike at the ruling death knight directly, this hidden iron gate serves as the primary staging point for surgical strikes against the Lich King's commanders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Stratholme Service Entrance located?",a="The entrance is situated at Eastwall Gate, along the northern mountains of the Eastern Plaguelands, just east of the main ruins of Stratholme. It is tucked into a stone archway along the fortified wall.",al={"service entrance location","where is back gate","strat side entrance map","how to find strat back door"}},{q="How does this entrance differ from the Stratholme Main Gate?",a="The Main Gate leads directly into the living and crusader-controlled ruins around King's Square, whereas the Service Entrance deposits you into Elders' Square, placing you on the doorstep of the undead-dominated wing and the road toward Slaughter Square.",al={"back door vs front door","service entrance difference","which strat entrance"}},{q="Why is it called the Service Entrance?",a="Before Stratholme fell, it was the commercial and logistical postern gate used by workers, couriers, and supply wagons to deliver goods into the city's infrastructure without congesting the monumental main plazas.",al={"why service entrance","service gate lore"}},{q="Who controls this part of the city?",a="The district beyond the gate is firmly held by the Scourge, overseen by Baron Rivendare and his acolytes, who maintain the ziggurats anchoring their dark magic within Elders' Square.",al={"who controls back gate","service entrance bosses","undead side leader"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For knights of the Light, this threshold leads straight into the defiled necromantic apparatus of the Scourge, offering a direct path to purge Rivendare and reclaim the holy city's fallen honor.",["class:Rogue"]="The service gate embodies classic tactical infiltration, allowing adventurers to bypass fortified battle lines and slip quietly into the city's utility corridors."},kw={"back door","baron rivendare","eastern plaguelands","eastwall gate","elders square","scourge","service entrance","stratholme"},rel={"subzone:stratholme","subzone:eastwall-gate","subzone:stratholme-main-gate","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Stratholme Service Entrance"}}
E["subzone:terrordale"] = {t="subzone",n="Terrordale",z="easternplaguelands",s="Terrordale is a ruined, ghost-haunted settlement nestled in the northwestern edge of the Eastern Plaguelands. Bordered by the blighted Plaguewood and the arachnid-infested Terrorweb Tunnel, the ruined town swarms with the Scourge and the restless dead.",h="Terrordale is a ruined, ghost-haunted settlement nestled in the northwestern edge of the Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Haunted Haven on the Wood's Edge",b="Once a quiet settlement in northern Lordaeron, Terrordale fell along with the rest of the kingdom to the Scourge. Today, the village stands in grim ruin near the mouth of the Terrorweb Tunnel. Its streets are choked with restless shades and wandering undead, while the surrounding trees of the Plaguewood encroach on its rotten timber. Amidst the desolation, only a handful of living eccentrics dare remain—such as the peculiar merchant Augustus the Touched and the ghost hunter Egan, who attempts to free the tortured spirits caught between worlds.",sp=0},{t="Spiritual Disturbance and Exorcism",b="The anguish of Terrordale's demise ran so deep that the physical world literally buckles beneath the torment of the spirit realm. Terrordale spirits linger in perpetual agony, bound to the earth by their tragic ends. Because of this concentrated spiritual corruption, seasoned paladins under the guidance of the Silver Hand and Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker are dispatched here to perform rites of judgment and sacrifice, banishing the torment as a sacred trial of holy discipline.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Terrordale?",a="Terrordale is an abandoned, ruined hamlet in the northwestern Eastern Plaguelands. Located just west of the Plaguewood and south of the Terrorweb Tunnel, it is thoroughly overrun by Scourge horrors and tormented ghosts.",al={"where is terrordale","what is this town","terrordale lore"}},{q="Who are the living people still in the town?",a="Two eccentric figures linger among the ruins: Egan, an intrepid ghost hunter trying to pacify and free the trapped spirits, and Augustus the Touched, a half-mad hermit and merchant obsessed with recovering his old ledgers and possessions.",al={"who is egan","who is augustus","living npcs in terrordale"}},{q="What connects this town to the paladin trials?",a="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker sends paladins seeking to bond with their holy warhorse charger to Terrordale. Paladins must use sanctified water to banish the tormented spirits here, demonstrating the spiritual resolve, judgment, and sacrifice required of an elite knight of the Light.",al={"paladin charger terrordale","exorcising terrordale","lord grayson shadowbreaker"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Terrordale serves as a crucial trial ground for veteran paladins; Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker requires candidates for the charger steed to venture into the ruined hamlet to exorcise its weeping spirits.",["race:Human"]="The broken houses of Terrordale offer a sobering reminder of northern Lordaeron's fall, where common citizens' spirits remain trapped in death within their own front yards."},kw={"augustus the touched","charger","eastern plaguelands","egan","grayson shadowbreaker","plaguewood","terrordale","terrorweb tunnel"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:plaguewood","subzone:terrorweb-tunnel","npc:lord-grayson-shadowbreaker","subzone:thondroril-river","subzone:northdale","topic:scourge","subzone:darkshire"},src={"Terrordale"}}
E["subzone:terrorweb-tunnel"] = {t="subzone",n="Terrorweb Tunnel",z="easternplaguelands",s="Terrorweb Tunnel is a subterranean passage carving through the mountains between Terrordale and the Thondroril River. Infested with the Scourge's undead nerubian crypt fiends, it forms a hazardous subterranean shortcut across the western border of the Eastern Plaguelands.",h="Terrorweb Tunnel is a subterranean passage carving through the mountains between Terrordale and the...",sec={{t="A Subterranean Infestation",b="Bored straight through the mountains flanking the Thondroril River, the Terrorweb Tunnel links the contaminated village of Terrordale with the riverbanks to the south. Rather than typical ghouls or skeletal sentries, this dark subterranean bypass is claimed entirely by crypt fiends—mummified nerubian arachnids raised into servitude by the Lich King. Traveling the length of the passage cuts out long circuits around the mountain slopes, but requires navigating thick webs and avoiding towering nerubian overseers that patrol the dark.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Terrorweb Tunnel lead?",a="The tunnel cuts directly through the mountain range northwest of Terrordale. Its northern entrance opens into Terrordale, while its southern mouth exits onto the rocky banks overlooking the Thondroril River.",al={"terrorweb tunnel path","where does terrorweb go","terrorweb connections"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the tunnel?",a="The tunnel is swarming with crypt fiends, the undead nerubian spider-lords of ancient Northrend raised into the Scourge. Among their ranks, formidable Nerubian Overseers occasionally stalk the tunnels, making travel exceptionally dangerous.",al={"terrorweb mobs","who lives in terrorweb tunnel","terrorweb tunnel monsters"}},{q="Who is nearby outside the tunnel?",a="The exiled paladin Tirion Fordring maintains a modest campsite along the Thondroril River, just near the southern mouth of the tunnel.",al={"who is outside terrorweb","tirion near terrorweb","npc near terrorweb tunnel"}},{q="Why are nerubians in the Plaguelands?",a="After the Lich King conquered the subterranean kingdom of Azjol-Nerub in Northrend, he reanimated fallen nerubians as crypt fiends. When the Scourge invaded Lordaeron, these arachnid shock troops were deployed south to enforce the Cult of the Damned's grip on the region.",al={"why crypt fiends here","nerubians in plaguelands"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The tunnel's southern mouth sits just steps from the exiled Highlord Tirion Fordring, whose presence near this festering hive serves as a solitary watch against the Scourge's creeping spread."},kw={"crypt fiends","nerubian","nerubian overseer","terrordale","terrorweb tunnel","thondroril river","tirion fordring"},rel={"subzone:terrordale","subzone:thondroril-river","npc:tirion-fordring","zone:easternplaguelands"},src={"Terrorweb Tunnel"}}
E["subzone:thalassian-pass"] = {t="subzone",n="Thalassian Pass",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Thalassian Pass is a mountain crossing on the northern edge of the Eastern Plaguelands, forming the historic threshold between Lordaeron and the elven kingdom of Quel'Thalas. Guarded by the remnants of an ancient elfgate, the way north remains sealed and overshadowed by the lingering ruin of the Third War.",h="The Thalassian Pass is a mountain crossing on the northern edge of the Eastern Plaguelands, forming the...",sec={{t="Gateway to the North",b="Carved into the rugged peaks separating the Plaguelands from Quel'Thalas, the Thalassian Pass long served as the main overland route connecting the high elves to the northern kingdoms of Lordaeron. Fortified with grand elfgates, it was meant to isolate the high elven kingdom from external threats. During the Third War, those very defenses were breached when the Scourge marched north under Prince Arthas, devastating the kingdom beyond. Today, the passage stands silent and impassable, heavily marked by the Scourge invasion that shattered the elven realm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Thalassian Pass lead?",a="The pass cuts directly through the northern mountain range of the Eastern Plaguelands, leading toward the southern borders of Quel'Thalas. Historically, travelers from Lordaeron used this route to enter the elven dominion.",al={"where does thalassian pass go","thalassian pass destination","what is behind the gate"}},{q="Can you enter Quel'Thalas through this gate right now?",a="No. The heavy portal and fortifications are sealed shut, cutting off northern travel between the plagued lands of Lordaeron and the ruins of Quel'Thalas.",al={"can i open thalassian pass","enter quel thalas classic","is thalassian pass open"}},{q="What happened to the defenses guarding the pass?",a="During the Third War, the Scourge bypassed and broke through the elfgates barring the road to Silvermoon, aided by the betrayal of the elven magister Dar'Khan Drathir. The defiled ruins and lingering banners bear witness to that assault.",al={"why is it ruined","who destroyed thalassian gate","scourge attack pass"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, especially those who recall the fall of Quel'Thalas alongside the Dark Lady, the sealed northern pass serves as a stark reminder of the Scourge's initial, merciless advance."},kw={"eastern plaguelands","elfgate","high elves","lordaeron","quel'thalas","scourge","thalassian pass"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","topic:horde"},src={"Thalassian Pass"}}
E["subzone:thondroril-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Thondroril River",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Thondroril River is a vital natural boundary separating the Western and Eastern Plaguelands. Originating in the mountains of Northern Lordaeron near the Terrorweb Tunnel, its blighted waters flow southward into Darrowmere Lake. Once a vibrant trade and travel waterway of the fallen kingdom, it is now flanked by monstrous Scourge beasts and the humble refuge of a legendary hermit.",h="The Thondroril River is a vital natural boundary separating the Western and Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A River Cut by Ruin",b="Before the fall of Lordaeron, the Thondroril served as an important waterway connecting northern holdings toward Stratholme and south to Darrowmere Lake. Today, the river marks the hazardous divide between the Western and Eastern Plaguelands. The waters carry the taint of the plague, and its banks are infested with giant maggots, plaguebats, diseased bears, and predatory snapjaws, turning what was once a scenic riverbed into a deadly crossing for travelers.",sp=0},{t="Watchers on the Bank",b="Though the wilderness along the Thondroril is harsh and unforgiving, it is not entirely devoid of hope. On the eastern bank, nestled in an unassuming, overgrown homestead, lives the exiled Paladin Tirion Fordring. Stripped of his titles and forced into hiding years ago, the former lord watches the rotting river and the ruin of his homeland from afar, testing the mettle and conscience of adventurers hardy enough to cross the blighted frontier.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the Thondroril River begin and end?",a="The river rises in the heights of Northern Lordaeron near the entrance of Terrorweb Tunnel, then flows south across the Plaguelands until it empties directly into Darrowmere Lake. Past the lake, the waterway continues south as the Darrowmere River.",al={"thondroril river path","where does thondroril flow","source of thondroril"}},{q="What dangerous creatures live along the riverbanks?",a="The plague has mutated the native wildlife into lethal monstrosities. Travelers regularly encounter devouring maggots, diseased plaguebears, massive vampire bats, crypt spiders, and river snapjaws stalking both banks.",al={"monsters near river","thondroril mobs","river threats"}},{q="Who is the old man living by the eastern shore?",a="The solitary figure in the dilapidated farmhouse on the eastern bank is Tirion Fordring, one of the original Knights of the Silver Hand. Exiled from the Alliance years before the Third War, he lives in quiet seclusion observing the Scourge.",al={"who is by the river","old hermit thondroril","thondroril questgiver"}},{q="Why does the river divide the two Plaguelands?",a="The Thondroril carved a wide natural gorge through central Lordaeron. When the kingdom collapsed into Scourge territory, cartographers and survivors began treating the river as the clear frontier dividing the Western and Eastern Plaguelands.",al={"western vs eastern border","plaguelands boundary"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The Thondroril River's eastern shore shelters Tirion Fordring, a founding father of the Silver Hand whose legacy still echoes despite his exile.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The damp, rotting riverbed nurtures hardy plague-tainted flora such as Sungrass, Arthas' Tears, and Plaguebloom near its murky shores."},kw={"darrowmere lake","eastern plaguelands","lordaeron","terrorweb tunnel","thondroril","thondroril river","tirion fordring","western plaguelands"},rel={"npc:tirion-fordring","zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:darrowmere-lake","subzone:terrorweb-tunnel","subzone:stratholme","topic:lordaeron","topic:second-war"},src={"Thondroril River"}}
E["subzone:tyr-s-hand"] = {t="subzone",n="Tyr's Hand",z="easternplaguelands",s="Tyr's Hand is a heavily fortified human stronghold situated in the southeastern hills of the Eastern Plaguelands. Long revered as an ancient holy site for the Church of the Holy Light, the city now serves as the primary regional bastion and supply hub for the zealous Scarlet Crusade.",h="Tyr's Hand is a heavily fortified human stronghold situated in the southeastern hills of the Eastern...",sec={{t="A City of Churches",b="Perched defensively in what was once Lordaeron's green Eastweald, Tyr's Hand is one of humanity's most ancient sacred sites. Named in memory of the legendary keeper Tyr, whose sacrifice and silver hand inspired northern legends, the settlement became known as a 'city of churches' as shrines and holy structures were raised across its grounds. Unlike the blight-rotted ruins that litter the rest of the Plaguelands, Tyr's Hand remains remarkably preserved behind formidable masonry, thick walls, and the towering silhouette of the Scarlet Basilica.",sp=0},{t="Fortress of the Scarlet Crusade",b="When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron during the Third War, Lord Valdelmar kept the city standing through sheer military vigilance and faith. After the Knights of the Silver Hand shattered into rival factions, Tyr's Hand aligned firmly with the Crimson dawn of the Scarlet Crusade. Today, it operates as an impenetrable base of operations led by High General Brigitte Abbendis and Valdelmar. Elite crusaders train within its abbey, heavily guarded couriers maintain communication with scarlet forces holding Stratholme, and the city ruthlessly rebuffs all outsiders who approach its gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the city called Tyr's Hand?",a="The city honors the heroic keeper Tyr, a figure of myth among the early northern humans. Legend tells that Tyr lost his hand battling a monstrous beast and replaced it with a hand of silver, inspiring humanity's earliest teachings on sacrifice and righteous justice.",al={"who is tyr","tyrs hand name meaning","origin of tyrs hand"}},{q="Why hasn't the Scourge overrun Tyr's Hand?",a="Tyr's Hand occupies a natural mountainous chokepoint and is shielded by formidable stone fortifications, barracks, and an abbey. In addition to defensive geography, the Scarlet Crusade maintains an elite, heavily armed standing garrison whose martial zeal and radiant holy magic have successfully repelled relentless Scourge assaults.",al={"why did tyrs hand survive","how is tyrs hand not undead","how does tyrs hand hold out"}},{q="Are travelers and adventurers welcome in Tyr's Hand?",a="No. The Scarlet Crusade has descended into xenophobic paranoia, viewing anyone outside their ranks as potential carriers of the undead plague or secret agents of the Scourge. Outsiders from both the Alliance and the Horde are attacked on sight.",al={"can i visit tyrs hand","is tyrs hand friendly","are scarlet crusaders friendly here"}},{q="What role did the city play during the Second War?",a="During the Second War, Alterac provocateurs secretly stoked a peasant revolt within Tyr's Hand to mask an orcish mining outpost nearby. After the Alliance and the Silver Hand subdued the unrest, Horde ogre magi heavily bombarded the city and sacked the neighboring bay to cut Quel'Thalas supply lines.",al={"second war tyrs hand","peasant revolt tyrs hand"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For holy warriors, seeing this ancient cradle of the Silver Hand twisted into a bastion of mad, unyielding Scarlet zealotry serves as a stark warning of what faith looks like when untempered by compassion.",["class:Priest"]="The abbey and Scarlet Basilica stand as magnificent architectural marvels of the early Church of the Holy Light, even if the clergy inside have traded pastoral healing for blind crusade."},kw={"abbendis","demetria","eastweald","holy light","scarlet basilica","scarlet crusade","tyr's hand","valdelmar"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-basilica","subzone:tyr-s-hand-abbey","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:stratholme","topic:scourge"},src={"Tyr's Hand"}}
E["subzone:tyr-s-hand-abbey"] = {t="subzone",n="Tyr's Hand Abbey",z="easternplaguelands",s="Tyr's Hand Abbey is a well-maintained sanctuary nestled within the fortified bastion of Tyr's Hand in the southeastern Eastern Plaguelands. Controlled by the zealots of the Scarlet Crusade, it serves as an auxiliary house of worship and study alongside the grand Scarlet Basilica.",h="Tyr's Hand Abbey is a well-maintained sanctuary nestled within the fortified bastion of Tyr's Hand in the...",sec={{t="Sanctuary of the Zealots",b="While the imposing Scarlet Basilica dominates the skyline of Tyr's Hand, the abbey provides a quieter, functional center of devotion and martial doctrine for the Scarlet Crusade. Its architecture closely mirrors traditional Holy Light foundations such as Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest, featuring a central Main Hall flanked by a Hall of Arms and a dedicated Library Wing. Despite the relentless horrors of the Plaguelands, the Crusade maintains the abbey with meticulous care, fiercely defending its cloisters from all outsiders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Tyr's Hand Abbey used for?",a="It serves as a secondary religious and logistical facility for the Scarlet Crusade in Tyr's Hand. While the grand Basilica hosts major ceremonies, the abbey provides living, training, and study quarters with its Hall of Arms and Library Wing.",al={"what is this building","tyrs hand abbey purpose","what happens in the abbey"}},{q="Why does it look like Northshire Abbey?",a="Both structures were built following standard Lordaeron and Stormwind architectural designs for Church of the Holy Light monastic compounds, dividing the building into a main assembly hall, a martial training wing, and an archive of sacred texts.",al={"northshire clone","why does it look like northshire","abbey layout"}},{q="Who controls the abbey right now?",a="The abbey is under the total control of the Scarlet Crusade. Like the rest of the heavily fortified city of Tyr's Hand, it is fiercely defended by crusader soldiers, priests, and paladins who attack anyone not bearing their colors.",al={"who owns tyrs hand abbey","is scarlet crusade here"}},{q="Can players ring the bell in the belfry?",a="The abbey features a bell in its tower that shows an interaction cursor, similar to the alarm bells found in maritime towns like Booty Bay, though striking it currently produces no sound or reaction.",al={"church bell","belfry bell","interact with bell"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For holy warriors, the abbey represents the tragic corruption of the Silver Hand's legacy: a once-hallowed place of prayer turned into a bastion of fanaticism and bloodlust.",["class:Priest"]="The Library Wing holds remnants of classical Holy Light doctrine, though preserved through the skewed and obsessive filter of the Scarlet Crusade."},kw={"eastern plaguelands","hall of arms","library wing","scarlet basilica","scarlet crusade","tyr's hand abbey","tyrs hand"},rel={"subzone:tyr-s-hand","subzone:scarlet-basilica","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:easternplaguelands"},src={"Tyr's Hand Abbey"}}
E["subzone:undercroft"] = {t="subzone",n="Undercroft",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Undercroft is an ancient burial crypt nestled in the southwestern hills of the Eastern Plaguelands. Once a dignified tomb of Lordaeron, it has been desecrated by a band of undead trolls under the command of Zaeldarr the Outcast. Amid the defiled catacombs lies an ersatz grave dug long ago to feign the death of the exiled paladin Tirion Fordring.",h="The Undercroft is an ancient burial crypt nestled in the southwestern hills of the Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Desecrated Sepulcher",b="Carved into the rugged bluffs southwest of Corin's Crossing, the Undercroft was originally built as a final resting place for the honored dead of Lordaeron. The fall of the kingdom stripped away its sanctity, and the tomb is now infested by a band of savage undead trolls. Led by the hulking monstrosity Zaeldarr the Outcast, these ghoulish marauders use the underground halls as a redoubt from which to stalk the Plaguelands, even daring to raid the grave pits of Light's Hope Chapel to gather raw corpses for their sinister practices.",sp=0},{t="A Pretender's Tomb",b="Beyond its monstrous squatter, the Undercroft harbors a poignant secret of the Second War era: a mock grave bearing the name of Tirion Fordring. Following his trial for treason and subsequent exile, Fordring's allies staged his symbolic burial here to allow his family to maintain their standing while letting the fallen paladin slip into hiding. Within this earthen deception rests a personal memento from Tirion's past, hidden away where only those who know the truth would dare to search.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Undercroft?",a="The Undercroft is a burial crypt situated in the southwestern region of the Eastern Plaguelands. Originally constructed to inter local nobility and fallen soldiers of Lordaeron, it has fallen into ruin and is now occupied by undead horrors.",al={"where is undercroft","what is this crypt","undercroft epl"}},{q="Who occupies the crypt now?",a="The crypt is infested by a band of undead trolls led by a massive undead dire troll known as Zaeldarr the Outcast. They use the tunnels as a lair between scavenging raids across the region.",al={"who is inside undercroft","undercroft mobs","trolls in undercroft"}},{q="Why are there undead trolls in the Eastern Plaguelands?",a="While the Scourge primarily raised humans and elves in northern Lordaeron, troll tribes such as the Mossflayer and Witherbark dwell nearby. Undead trolls like Zaeldarr and his reanimated followers roam the bluffs, pillaging burial sites and preying on unwary travelers.",al={"why trolls here","zaeldarr lore","undead trolls epl"}},{q="Why is Tirion Fordring's name on a grave here?",a="The grave is an ersatz, or false, resting place. After Tirion was stripped of his rank and exiled by the Alliance of Lordaeron, a mock burial was arranged at the Undercroft so his family could preserve their honor and claim his death while he lived secretly in hiding.",al={"tirion grave","is tirion dead","fordring tomb"}},{q="Why do the Undercroft trolls raid Light's Hope Chapel?",a="Zaeldarr the Outcast occasionally leads nighttime raids against the grave pits outside Light's Hope Chapel. His objective is to unearth and steal newly buried corpses to bolster his own band or feed their morbid appetites.",al={"zaeldarr raids","grave pit raid","trolls light's hope"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For holy warriors, entering the Undercroft means witnessing both the tragic mock burial of the exiled hero Tirion Fordring and the foul desecration of sacred crypts by Zaeldarr's vile brood.",["race:Troll"]="Troll travelers will view Zaeldarr the Outcast and his undead kindred as a grim, perverted mockery of troll traditions and the sacred rites owed to deceased ancestors."},kw={"crypt","dire troll","eastern plaguelands","grave","light's hope","the outcast","tirion fordring","undercroft","zaeldarr"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","npc:tirion-fordring","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","topic:argent-dawn","topic:troll","topic:light"},src={"Undercroft"}}
E["subzone:zul-mashar"] = {t="subzone",n="Zul'Mashar",z="easternplaguelands",s="Zul'Mashar is an ancient forest troll settlement tucked into the northeastern corner of the Eastern Plaguelands. Formerly the proud capital of the Mossflayer tribe, it has deteriorated into a desolate ruin following continuous wars with human kingdoms and the devastation of the Plague of Undeath. Today, its remaining defenders face an insidious collapse as the Scourge works from within to turn them into undead thralls.",h="Zul'Mashar is an ancient forest troll settlement tucked into the northeastern corner of the Eastern...",sec={{t="A Falling Stronghold",b="Long before the Scourge swept across northern Lordaeron, Zul'Mashar served as the seat of power for the Mossflayer forest trolls. Constant border skirmishes against the humans of Lordaeron chipped away at their dominance, leaving their territories fractured. When the Plague of Undeath blanketed the region, it struck the Mossflayers just as mercilessly as it did their mortal enemies. While the great stepped ziggurat of Mazra'Alor still stands, Zul'Mashar is a hollow shell of its former glory. Commanded by Warlord Thresh'jin and Zul'Brin Warpbranch, the remaining trolls cling stubbornly to their ancient home, largely blind to the reality that Scourge influence is already seeping into their ranks and quietly transforming their kin into rotting monstrosities.",sp=0},{t="Infiltration from the Shadows",b="The true peril facing Zul'Mashar is not a direct siege by the Scourge, but a creeping rot from within. Even as the Mossflayers attempt to guard their ziggurat and maintain their independence in the ruined north, agents and covert rot spread through their population. With scouts like Infiltrator Hameya operating amid the ruins and their living warriors gradually succumbing to undeath, the once-proud stronghold stands on the verge of falling completely under the Lich King's sway without a single grand battle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who controls Zul'Mashar?",a="Zul'Mashar is held by the Mossflayer tribe of forest trolls, led by Warlord Thresh'jin alongside Zul'Brin Warpbranch. However, their hold is actively slipping as the undead plague infiltrates their society.",al={"who lives in zulmashar","zul mashar rulers","mossflayer leaders"}},{q="What is Mazra'Alor?",a="Mazra'Alor is the prominent stepped troll ziggurat situated within Zul'Mashar. It represents the architectural heart and spiritual center of the Mossflayer tribe's ancestral capital.",al={"mazraalor","zul mashar pyramid","troll ziggurat epl"}},{q="Why is Zul'Mashar in ruins?",a="Zul'Mashar was worn down by long, grinding conflicts against the human kingdom of Lordaeron before being ravaged by the Plague of Undeath. The blight ruined the surrounding land and left the Mossflayers isolated and weakened.",al={"why is zulmashar destroyed","what happened to zul mashar"}},{q="Are the trolls here allied with the Scourge?",a="No, the living Mossflayers are hostile to outsiders and fight to protect their ancestral lands. However, the Scourge is covertly infecting and converting their people into undead, steadily hollowing out the tribe from within.",al={"are mossflayers scourge","trolls working with scourge"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, witnessing the plight of the Mossflayers at Zul'Mashar is a grim reminder of the fate awaiting isolated tribes that cling to ancient hatreds rather than finding allies in a changing world.",["race:Undead"]="The Forsaken view Zul'Mashar with wary pragmatism, keeping an eye on whether the decaying Mossflayer tribe will resist or inevitably swell the ranks of the Scourge with fresh, zombified forest trolls."},kw={"eastern plaguelands","forest troll","hameya","mazra'alor","mossflayer","thresh'jin","warpbranch","zul'mashar"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","topic:troll","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Zul'Mashar"}}
E["zone:easternplaguelands"] = {t="zone",n="Eastern Plaguelands",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Eastern Plaguelands represent the devastated heart of the fallen Kingdom of Lordaeron, suffocated under Scourge blight, toxic mists, and corrupted fungal growths. Stratholme looms in the north as the undead power base in the region, while the zealous Scarlet Crusade entrenches in the east. Amid the nightmare, Light's Hope Chapel stands as a resolute, neutral sanctuary for anyone brave enough to fight back.",h="The Eastern Plaguelands represent the devastated heart of the fallen Kingdom of Lordaeron, suffocated under...",sec={{t="A Land in Ruin",b="Once known as the fertile Eastweald, this region was the agricultural spine of northern Lordaeron, anchored by the great metropolis of Stratholme and prosperous towns like Darrowshire and Corin's Crossing. During the Third War, Prince Arthas purged Stratholme after discovering its grain supply had been laced with the Plague of Undeath. Following the kingdom's collapse, the Scourge's dark magic ran unchecked. The soil turned brown and rotten, ordinary flora warped into colossal mushrooms, and an eerie orange mist settled across the valleys.",sp=0},{t="A War on Three Fronts",b="Stratholme serves as the southern seat of Scourge authority in Lordaeron, commanded by Baron Rivendare under the direction of the lich Kel'Thuzad. Defying the undead from the southeast is the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, which has fortified the town of Tyr's Hand and assaults Stratholme's scarlet bastions. Their dogmatic hatred extends beyond the dead to any living traveler who crosses their borders. To the north, the Mossflayer forest trolls of Zul'Mashar wage their own isolated, desperate campaigns, caught in the crossfire of the greater conflict.",sp=0},{t="Bastions of the Living",b="Survival in the Eastern Plaguelands requires careful footing. The neutral Argent Dawn operates out of Light's Hope Chapel in the far east, offering a safe haven, essential supplies, and flight routes to both Alliance and Horde champions. Beyond the chapel, the two factions actively clash over four strategic ruined towers—Crown Guard, Eastwall, Northpass, and Plaguewood—wrestling for area-wide tactical dominance to bolster their fighters against the undead horrors.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What caused the sky and trees to look so sick?",a="The landscape suffers from the concentrated effects of the Cult of the Damned's Plague of Undeath. Left unchecked after the Third War, the foul necromantic magic blighted the earth, mutated local wildlife, choked the atmosphere in an unnatural orange smog, and transformed natural forests into grotesque fungal groves like the Plaguewood.",al={"why is the sky orange","why giant mushrooms","eastern plaguelands corruption"}},{q="Where can I find a safe haven or flight path here?",a="Light's Hope Chapel, located along the eastern edge of the zone, is the main sanctuary. Maintained by the Argent Dawn, it provides flight paths connecting to Undercity, Ironforge, Chillwind Camp, and the Hinterlands, welcoming both Alliance and Horde travelers.",al={"epl safe zone","where is flight path epl","friendly town eastern plaguelands"}},{q="Who controls the city of Stratholme?",a="Stratholme is divided by ongoing warfare. The majority of the burning ruins are ruled by the Scourge under Baron Rivendare, serving Kel'Thuzad. However, the Scarlet Crusade maintains an aggressive garrison within the western district, waging a relentless and bloody siege against the undead forces.",al={"who leads stratholme","stratholme bosses lore","what is in stratholme"}},{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade hostile to outside adventurers?",a="Following the fall of Lordaeron and the fracturing of the Silver Hand, the Scarlet Crusade succumbed to rampant zealotry and paranoia. Convinced that all outsiders harbor the taint of the plague or consort with the undead, they attack any non-members who approach their strongholds, such as Tyr's Hand.",al={"why does scarlet crusade attack me","tyrs hand hostile","scarlet crusade red"}},{q="What happened to the town of Darrowshire?",a="During the Third War, Scourge forces led by the death knight Marduk the Black and the ghoul Horgus the Ravager assaulted the town. Although paladin Davil Crokford and Captain Joseph Redpath fought valiantly, Redpath's soul was corrupted by necromancy, turning him into an instrument of slaughter against his own people. The town now lies in haunted ruins.",al={"darrowshire lore","fall of darrowshire","who destroyed darrowshire"}},{q="Why are Alliance and Horde fighting over the ruined towers?",a="Scattered across the zone are four ruined Lordaeron watchtowers: Crown Guard, Eastwall, Northpass, and Plaguewood. Both factions contend for their control to claim strategic defensive outposts and area-wide tactical boons that aid their forces against the surrounding undead.",al={"epl towers","a game of towers","plaguelands tower objectives"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The fallen realm of Lordaeron holds profound tragedy for the Silver Hand, from the site of Arthas's dark turning in Stratholme to the valiant last stand at Light's Hope Chapel.",["race:Undead"]="The Eastern Plaguelands represent both the birthplace of the Scourge menace and a vital frontline where the Forsaken strike back against their former masters and the Scarlet zealots.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, venturing into the Plaguelands is a solemn pilgrimage to reclaim and honor the devastated remnants of their former northern allies.",["profession:Herbalism"]="This blighted region is one of the exceptionally rare places to gather volatile, high-tier herbs like Arthas' Tears, Plaguebloom, and Black Lotus.",["profession:Mining"]="Veins of Truesilver, Mithril, and Rich Thorium are embedded across the corrupted hillsides and dangerous Scourge-infested valleys."},kw={"argent dawn","darrowshire","eastern plaguelands","kelthuzad","lights hope chapel","nathanos","plaguewood","rivendare","scarlet crusade","scourge","stratholme","tyrs hand"},rel={"zone:westernplaguelands","subzone:stratholme","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","subzone:darrowshire","subzone:plaguewood","subzone:corin-s-crossing","subzone:marris-stead","subzone:thondroril-river"},src={"Eastern Plaguelands (Classic)","Eastern Plaguelands"}}
